2 CONT
2 CONT History - His father and mother come to Utah in 1847 and settled in the 19th ward of Salt Lake City. He came to Utah in September 1848 in the Willard Richards Company. His eldest son Ferdinand, and his brother Philemon were member
2 CONC s of the Mormon battalion. Philemon was a general in the Mormon battalion. His sister Phoebe Lodemia accompanied it part of the way as a washerwoman and cook, although she was only fourteen. His mother died in 1863 and his father 
2 CONC died 1877. His father is buried in Salt Lake Cemetery. He died at his father's home in Salt Lake City
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Pioneer Heritage, Vol. 18, p. 134
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin Merrill was born February 18, 1806, at Byron, Genessee County, New York. He and his wife Camilla Wirick Merrill came to Utah September 1848, with the Willard Richards Company. They established a home at Smithfield, Cache Co
2 CONC unty, Utah and helped to pioneer this area. He was called to the Las Vegas Mission in 1856 where his knowledge of farming and raising fine horses was needed. Upon his release he returned to Smithfield where he died January 14, 188
2 CONC 7. 
