1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=89461200 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. EMMA COZZENS DIES IN OGDEN
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Emma Cozzens, former resident and pioneer lady of this county, died at the Dee Hospital in Ogden Thursday morning from the effects of gall stones.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Cozzens was born in Salt Lake City on July 9, 1853 and came to Bear Lake County with her parents, who were among the first company of settlers here. She was a lady of pleasing disposition and made friends of all people she me
2 CONC t. Her many friends and acquaintances in this vicinity will be grieved to learn of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. E. I Rich of Ogden, Utah; 
2 CONT
2 CONT W. E. Cozzens of Border, Wyo.;
2 CONT
2 CONT O. M. Cozzens of Edwards, N. Y.; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark Cozzens of Midvale, Utah; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Cozzens of Afton, Wyo.; and
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mrs. H. C. Hancock of Port Chester, N. Y. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also survived by thirty five grand children and four great grand children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The remains arrived here this morning on No. 6 and the funeral services will be held at the Montpelier Stake Tabernacle Sunday at 12:30. Interment will be made in the Montpelier Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in Bear Lake County News in Montpelier, Bear Lake County, Idaho, on Saturday, August 4, 1923 on page 1
2 CONT
