1 NAME Lucy Ann /Merrill/
2 GIVN Lucy Ann
2 SURN Merrill
2 _MARNM Merrill
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 JUN 1860
2 ADDR
3 CITY Smithfield
3 STAE Utah Territory
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE MAY 1884
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint David
3 STAE Arizona
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 MAY 1884
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint David
3 STAE Arizona
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Married Seth Adelbert Merrill 10/28/1876 in Soda Springs, Idaho, and had 4 children.  After she died, Seth married Alice Rosemary Beebee and had 6 more children.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is another photo of Lucy Ann Merrill under the Media Tab above which features her and her husband probably on their wedding day.  Lucy Ann Merrill was born June 16, 1860, in Smithfield, Utah, the fourth of si
2 CONC x children born to Dudley Justin Merrill and Almira Huntsman.  Lucy Ann's family moved to Bear Lake, Idaho, before she was six years old.  Her mother died at age 32 in Salt Lake City when Lucy was only 7.  Her father married Ellen
2 CONC  Orliva Huntsman seven months later, April 4, 1868, in the Salt Lake Endowment House.  By this time Lucy's family had moved to Soda Springs, Idaho.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Soda Springs Lucy Ann fell in love with her first cousin once removed, Seth Adelbert Merrill (called Del or Delbert).  Del was the son of Philemon Christopher Merrill, Lucy Ann's great uncle.  Lucy Ann and Del were married in a
2 CONC  double wedding with other relatives on October 28, 1876, in Soda Springs, Idaho.  Lucy was 16 at this time and Del was 17.  A few weeks after their wedding, Brigham Young called the Merrill's to help settle southeastern Arizona. 
2 CONC  Lucy Ann and Del joined a company that included Lucy's parents, Del's parents, and other Merrill kin.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the journey a horse fell on Del's leg, causing it to break. The company delayed a week in northern Utah and finally Lucy Ann and Del took a train to Salt Lake City to have Del's leg set by a doctor.  The rest of the company con
2 CONC tinued south by wagons and met Lucy Ann and Del in Payson, Utah.  The company arrived in St. George, Utah, 10 days after the St. George Temple had been dedicated.  Lucy Ann and Del had their wedding sealed on Jan. 12, 1877.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Merrill's left St. George on January 17th and arrived on the Salt River near Tempe, Arizona, on March 7, 1877. After one summer on the Salt River, Lucy Ann and Del joined a company headed south and were among the first settler
2 CONC s of St. David, Arizona.  Lucy Ann and Del had three children in St. David: Almira, Seth Adelbert, and Orson Pratt.  Lucy Ann became a counselor in the presidency of the first Mutual Improvement Association in St. David. She died 
2 CONC May 8, 1884, at age 23. Her baby was three months old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Unpublished autobiography of Cyrena Dustin
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. "Patriarchs: Phileomon Christopher Merrill." The 25th Stake of Zion (On record at Harold B. Lee Library, Brigham Young University, Provo, Utah).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Ann Merrill - One Minute Stories...From the book:  James/Hatch One Minute Histories covering 200 Years and 45 Lives compiled by Daryl James, Phoenix, Arizona, December, 1994:
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Family Search.org
