1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-1086,00.html Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868 Edward Hunter - Jacob Foutz Company (1847)]  Age 12
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: 19 June 1847 Arrival: 1 October 1847
2 CONT
2 CONT Company Information: 155 individuals and 59 wagons were in the company when it began its journey from the outfitting post on the Elkhorn River about 27 miles west of Winter Quarters, Nebraska. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=22027387 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Dec. 10, 1835 Shelby Township Macomb County
2 CONT
2 CONT Michigan, USA Death: 	Jan. 22, 1915 Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT William Wallace Merrill is the son of Justin Jared Merrill and Annie Lovina Manchester. he was among the early LDS Pioneers and had lived at Nauvoo for a time.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lucy Maria Williams at Salt Lake City in 1857. They had 14 children, 9 of whom lived to maturity.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried with his wife in the Bluffdale City Cemetery in Bluffdale, Utah. 
2 CONT
