1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The above photo was found on Find A Grave.com and supposedly depicts Adelaide Lois "Addie" Rollins Colton, and her two cousins, Ida Bingham and Edwin Florentine Bingham.  Find A Grave shows that Adelaide Lois "Addi
2 CONC e" Rollins Colton was the daughter of James Henry Rollins (1816-1899) and his first wife, Eveline Walker Rollins (1823-1912), however, I believe she was the daughter of James Henry and his plural wife, Hannah Hulmes Rollins (1833-
2 CONC 1896).  According to Find A Grave.com, Adelaide married Joseph Philander Colton (1856-1934), the son of Charles Edwin Colton (1834-1916) and Mary Anne Kelting Colton (1838-1924).  Their son, Henry Leslie "Harry" Colton (1890-1918)
2 CONC  was born in Santa Rosa, Sonoma County, California, and while serving his country in France with the U.S. Army during World War I, he died due to spinal meningitis.  He was buried in the Forest Lawn Memorial Park Cemetery in Glend
2 CONC ale, Los Angeles County, California.  His headstone reads: "Died in France."
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida and Edwin were the children of Phebe Jane Burk Bingham, who was the daughter of James Henry Rollins' mother, Keziah Keturah Van Benthuysen Rollins, and her second husband, John Mathias Burk.  James Henry Rollins father, and Ke
2 CONC ziah's first husband, John Porter Rollins died in 1820 when the boat load of cattle he was taking from New York to Canada sank during a bad storm on Lake Erie.  All on board perished except for one person.  After John Porter Rolli
2 CONC ns death, Keziah sent her three children to live with her sister, Elizabeth Van Benthuysen Gilbert ,and her husband, Sidney Gilbert, who had no children.  They lived in Ohio until the entire family joined the Mormon Church in the 
2 CONC 1830's and migrated west with the Saints along with Keziah Keturah Van Benthuysen Rollins Burk.
