1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edward Bunker Company (1856)    Age at Departure: 23    Head of Household
2 CONT
2 CONT Traveled with    Martha Cozzens (Age: 23
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Cozzens&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSst=53&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=31715761&df=all& Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	May 17, 1833, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Oct. 13, 1905 Byron Big Horn County Wyoming, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT son of Diana Thomas & James Cozzens, married Martha Cozzens, and Emily Almira Merrill, and Sarah Jane Perkins
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cozzens 1833-1905
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cozzens was born 17 May 1833 in High Cross, Freystrop, Pembroke, Wales to James Cozzens & Diana Thomas. John was the oldest child in a family of 7 children. At an early age John went to work in the coal mines to help support 
2 CONC his family. When John was 12 years old his father and brother were killed in a mining accident. John joined the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints just before his 23 birthday in Feb 1856. He came to America with his cousi
2 CONC n Martha who had also joined the church. They crossed the plains in a handcart company made up of mostly Welsh speaking people. John married his cousin Martha Cozzens on 5 July 1856 on the journey across the plains. As they crosse
2 CONC d the plains food ran short and was rationed Martha became ill and was unable to walk, John pulled her many weary miles across the plains. Upon reaching the Salt Lake Valley, John and Martha first settled in Davis County, Utah, ne
2 CONC xt Hyrum, Cache Valley, Utah where they lived until 1863. They were called by Brigham Young to help colonize the Bear Lake Valley, John was instrumental in the development of Montpelier, Idaho. After 14 years of marriage John and 
2 CONC Martha had been blessed with no children. They divorced in 1870. John entered into the practice of plural marriage and married Emily Almira Merrill and Sarah Jane Perkins. Both reared large families,and both lived to be seventy ye
2 CONC ars of age. When John was 67 years old he was asked to go help settle the Big Horn Basin in Wyoming. In 1900 the family of Sarah Jane and John came to Byron in 3 stages. Emily and her family stayed in Montpelier, thinking they wou
2 CONC ld come later. During the 5 years which John spent in Byron before his death, John helped build up the town of Byron and he worked on other projects of development in the Big Horn Basin area such as helping to build the Northfork 
2 CONC and Yellowstone Park roads and helping build the railroads in the area. The Saints drank the Shoshone River water and some died of typhoid fever as a result. John Cozzens died of typhoid fever on the 13th of October 1905. at the a
2 CONC ge of 72 years. He died at his home in Byron, Wyoming. His son Luke who was 21 died of typhoid three days later. Two years later his youngest son, Golden, who was ten years old, died of diphtheria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In speaking of their father, his children remember certain outstanding characteristics about him. He was a very strong man physically. He was a man who never judged others. He was quiet about his religion, but very sincere. He nev
2 CONC er shouted nor made a fuss or preached on what others should do when he didn't do those things himself. He was trustworthy and very honest. He was always on hand to help others when he thought the need was sincere. He followed his
2 CONC  inclinations regardless of what others might say.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouses:
2 CONT
2 CONT   Emily Almira Merrill Cozzens (1853 - 1923)
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sarah Jane Perkins Cozzens (1854 - 1925)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Emily Almira Cozzens Rich (1871 - 1954)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   John W Cozzens (1873 - 1916)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   James Dudley Cozzens (1874 - 1901)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sarah Dianna Cozzens Burrington (1875 - 1949)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Matthew Cozzens (1878 - 1969)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Lucy Cozzens (1878 - 1879)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Mark Cozzens (1883 - 1949)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Luke Cozzens (1884 - 1905)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Joseph Francis Cozzens (1886 - 1964)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Paul Cozzens (1888 - 1960)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Mary Lucile Cozzens Hancock (1891 - 1976)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Milton Jesse Cozzens (1891 - 1923)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Martha Lapries Cozzens Palmer (1894 - 1955)*
2 CONT
2 CONT   Golden Cozzens (1897 - 1907)*
2 CONT
