1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Matilda Colburn was one of Francis Martin Pomeroy's two plural wives.  Sarah Matilda Colburn's parents were Thomas Colburn (1801-1887) and Sarah Bower.  Thomas Colburn's parents were Hannah Hamilton and Jonat
2 CONC han Colburn.  Hannah was born in Sussex County, New Jersey.  She and Jonathan married on August 2, 1792 Sussex County, New Jersey.  Hannah died at Rose Wayne County, New York age 81.  She was buried at Ferguson's Corners Galen Twp
2 CONC . Wayne County, New York.  Hannah's parent's were Thomas Hamilton and Sarah Westfall.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hamilton and wife Sarah Westfall were traveling with their friends and all their children when Joseph Brearley and Sarah Westfall drowned trying to cross the Swatara River in Pennsylvania.  Then Lydia Colburn Brearley and T
2 CONC homas Hamilton married and had several more children.  They were all on their way to Crowland, Canada, where Joseph Brearley's widowed mother and children were living.  She had moved there one year after her husband died in New Yo
2 CONC rk.  They never made it there, and Lydia and Thomas stayed in the U.S. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Colburn's sister Sarah Colburn married Jonathan Hampton.  Their son also named Jonathan married Julia Foster.  Jonathan and Julia's son was named Brigham Young Hampton named after his Godfather Brigham Young. Julia divorced 
2 CONC her husband and married Brigham Young.  She was his 34th wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hamilton above is buried at the same cemetery as Brigham Young's mother Abigail Howe Young at White Settlement Cemetery, Lansing, Tompkins County, New York, with his second wife Lydia Colburn.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Colburn Brearley Hamilton's brother was Jonathan Colburn who married Hannah Hamilton, Sarah Matilda Colburn Pomeroy's grandparents.  Lydia and her brother Jonathan Colburn's parents were John Colburn and Sarah Hoagland.  Sar
2 CONC ah Hoagland's parents were Christopher Hoagland and Catalyntje Schenck.  Christopher's parent's were Christopher Hoagland and Helena Middagh.  Helena's parents were (Aert Anthonize Middagh and Brechte Hansen Bergen) daughter of Ha
2 CONC ns Hansen Bergen and Sarah Rapalje.  Sarah Rapalje was the first European woman born in the New Netherlands (New York).  Her parents were Joris Rapalje and Catalina Trico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted on Find A Grave.com by Vicky Moon on 23 Oct 2010 with some minor edits.
