2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Ursulia was born in Salt Lake City, Utah, July 27, 1860. Her father was Francis M. Pomeroy, a member of the original band of pioneers who entered the Salt Lake Valley in 1847. Her mother was Sarah M. Colbourn, who emigrated t
2 CONC o Utah with her parents in 1848, and became the plural wife of Brother Pomeroy. Being of a high-spirited nature Sarah did not take kindly to that principle. President Brigham Young, who was familiar with all the circumstances surr
2 CONC ounding the case, sent for Sarah and gave her a blessing. He promised her in the name of the Lord that if she would remain true to the covenants she had made with her husband, she would bring forth a child whose posterity would ex
2 CONC tend an influence for good throughout Zion. Shortly after this prediction was made, Mary Ursulia was born. The mother felt that this child had been given to her in fulfillment of the promise made by President Young. _____
2 CONT
