1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of CAPTAIN.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A090041  DAR Ancestor #  A090041]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR# [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_descendants/?action=list&MyPrimary_Seqn=212177&MyLineageCount=1&Control_Min_Seqn=212177 A090041] shows '''Captain David Phelps''' served in the Connecticut militia and was i
2 CONC n the battles of Ticonderoga and Long Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain David Phelps''' settled in Turkey Hill in Simsbury, Conn.  He was a soldier in the Revolutionary War. His name is found many times in manuscript volumes in the state archives. He appears in state record of "Connecticut 
2 CONC Men in the Revolution" in 1776 Woodward's Brigade as Lt. in 2nd Company, also as Lt. in pay roll in Danbury Alarm, and also in the New Haven Alarm in [brother] Captain Noah Phelps's Company in 1779. He served under his brother Noa
2 CONC h Phelps, at the capture of Ticonderoga, 1775. He was Lieutenant at the Battle of Long Island, where he was taken prisoner, and was Captian when Tryon invaded the Colony. PBP pp9  He was married to Abigail Griswold on 7 Apr 1753 i
2 CONC n Simsbury, CT. 77 yrs old at his death.
