1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-13440,00.html Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868 Henry Ettleman Company (1853)]  Age 12
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: unknown Arrival: 1 October 1853
2 CONT
2 CONT Company Information: 40 individuals and 11 wagons were in the company when it began its journey from the outfitting post at Keokuk, Iowa. They left the Missouri River on July 1. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Perpetual Emigrating Fund
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=22027756 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Sep. 22, 1840 Herefordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Nov. 7, 1930 Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Maria Williams-Merrill was born in Weston Beggard, Hereford, England. She was the daughter of Benjamin Williams and Mary Ann Rock who joined the LDS church in England and came to Nauvoo to join the Saints. Benjamin died in Na
2 CONC voo in 1842 so Lucy grew up with a step-father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy later married William Wallace Merrill on the 31st of August 1857 in Salt Lake City. They had 14 children, 9 of which lived to maturity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy is buried in the Bluffdale City cemetery in Utah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
