1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.1857ironcountymilitia.com/index.php?title=Nephi_Johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-3551,00.html Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868 Willard Richards Company (1848)]  Age 14
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: 3 July 1848 Arrival: 10-19 October 1848
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-24377,00.html 	Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868 William Budge Company (1860)]  Age 26
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: 20 July 1860 Arrival: 5 October 1860
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=johnson&GSfn=nephi&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSst=35&GScnty=1962&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=9263771&df=all& Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Dec. 12, 1833 Kirtland Lake County Ohio, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jun. 21, 1919 Mesquite Clark County Nevada, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Joel H. Johnson and Annie Johnson. Baptized in May, 1842, by John Smith and migrated to Utah in 1848 (F. D. Richards' Company).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was acquainted with Joseph Smith, who stayed at the family home many times and he endured the persecution of those early days.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1851- 53 he lived at Cedar City, Utah; one of the first settlers in Iron county. He was called on an Indian mission and for many years after that he worked diligently in settling the valleys along the Rio Virgen and the Muddy
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1858 he went out with Col. Wm. H. Dame's exploring company to explore the desert west of Utah, and Bro. Johnson led some of the party as far west as Death Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same year he led an exploring party and built the road into Upper Virgen valley, locating the town of Virgen City, where he lived for fourteen years. While a resident he acted as presiding Elder, acting Bishop and Bishop's cou
2 CONC nselor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871 he moved to Kanab, Kane county, Utah, where he was first counselor to the Bishop; he also served three terms as county commissioner, acted as town president for several years, was superintendent of waterworks three years a
2 CONC nd road commissioner ten years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In January, 1856, while living at Cedar City, he married Mandana R. Merrill, who bore him ten children and in October, 1860, he married Conradina A. Mariger, who bore him sixteen children. In 1889 he married Mrs. Bodel M. Jensen, 
2 CONC a widow with six children, who also bore him one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT (LDS Bio. Encyclopedia 3: 131) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
