1 NAME Reuben /Collett/
2 GIVN Reuben
2 SURN Collett
2 _MARNM Collett
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Smithfield City Cemetery (Plot C_71_1)
2 ADDR
3 CITY Smithfield
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 JUL 1839
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 16 JAN 1920
2 ADDR
3 CITY Smithfield
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Daniel Collett and Esther Jones
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Elthurah Roseltha Merrill, 17 Jan 1861, Smithfield, Cache, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT History - Reuben was an Indian War Veteran - Lemhi, Idaho. He lost his arm in the first threshing machine brought to Smithfield, Utah. A doctor came up from Logan and then said he needed to return to Logan for his tools. A man sai
2 CONC d that he had meat cutting tools. They were used to remove the lower part of Reuben's arm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After he healed he became a teamster and helped with the move of the Chinese from Corine, Utah to Helena, Montana to work in the mines. The people who owned the mines wanted the Chinese to drop off the wagon before they arrived at
2 CONC  the mines because he was paid per person that he hauled in. The Chinese thought because Reuben had only one arm that they could get away faster, but he grabbed the reins, grabbed his gun, and shot into the air. This scared the Ch
2 CONC inese and they did not run away. He moved the family to Circleville where he was friends with Butch Cassidy aka George Leroy Parker. They moved to Gallup, New Mexico and then to the Uintah Basin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage to Elthurah Merrill was the first marriage in Smithfield in 1861.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=179073 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 9 2017, 22:24:08 UTC''
