1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The above photo is from Family Search.org and depicts left to right, Philander Clarence Hardy, husband of Lydia Merrill Hardy, her sister-in-law, Marie Brinegar Merrill, and her brother, Irven Collett Merrill.  The
2 CONC re are a couple of other photos of Lydia and her husband under the Media Tab above.  The following information was also from Family Search and was written by one of her grandchildren:  I remember Grandma Hardy as being very strict
2 CONC ...a no-nonsense kind of grandma.  But her skin was very soft and she always smelled sweet, like baby powder.  I remember watching her do laundry with her wringer washing machine then hang the clothes on the line outside to dry.  
2 CONC I loved watching that.  She was a great cook.  My dad says that's why he married her daughter.  A favorite recipe of mine that she gave me was her holiday prune cake.  Even though I have the recipe in her own handwriting, I cannot
2 CONC  get my prune cake to taste like hers.  Maybe she had a secret ingredient.  Grandma liked to watch pro wrestling and roller derby on TV. And she loved the Lawrence Welk show.  In fact, she was killed in a car accident on her 80th 
2 CONC birthday going to see Lawrence Welk.
