1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=21420784
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Roxana was born in Irasburg, Orleans, Vermont, died American Fork, Utah, Utah.  She was the daughter of Nathaniel Leavitt and Deborah Delano.  She married Benjamin Fletcher, 13 Apr 1838.  She married John Huntsman, 23 Jun 1841, Na
2 CONC uvoo, Hancock, Illinois.  She married William Snow, 12 Mar 1853, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah.  She had at least 2 children with John Huntsman, Salena and Ellen, and they were listed in Iowa, Piottawattamie County, in the Annot
2 CONC ated Record of U.S. Census in 1850.  Roxana was 31, Salena, 6, and Ellen, 2 years old.  With William Snow, she had 2 more children, Melissa Leavitt Snow Greenwood, 1855-1925 and John Leavitt Snow, 1857-1916.  In the 1860 census th
2 CONC ey were living in Lehi, Utah, and were listed as follows in the census record:  William Snow, 58, Roxana, 41, Celena, 16, Ellen, 12, Melissa, 5, and John, 3 years old.  Her daughter Selena, married James Chipman, and they were lis
2 CONC ted in the 1870 census for American Fork, Utah, as follows:  James Chipman, 32, Selena, 26, James, 10, Alfonzo, 7, Stephen, 6, Sarah, 5, Washburn, 3 and Blanch, 1 year old.  Roxana was 52, Melissa, 15, and John, 12 years old.  Rox
2 CONC ana died 11 years later in June of 1881 in American Fork, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
