1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Summary of 50th anniversary article in paper:  Born 9/17/1865. He came with his parents to a farm near Grant, IA, Montgomery County when he was 5 from Lafayette County WI. They moved in spring of 1881 to Shelby Cou
2 CONC nty, IA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Ella Swinehart in Feb 1889. They moved immediately to their home in Lincoln Township. When they came to the farm there was not a single tree there and the improvements were very poor. They planted tress and toiled together
2 CONC  through the years, doing other things which have made for a comfortable home. Only 3 farms in the neighborhood are occupied by the same families who resided on them 50 years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Children were born to the couple. Velma Evans of Corning, Vernor Westrope of Lincoln Nebraska, and Doris L who passed away in infancy. 2 nephews of Mrs. Westrope were reared in the home until grown. They are Herbert Kemp (Winneb
2 CONC ago, MN) and Lawrence Kemp (Cumberland - assume IA?). 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Obituary:  9th child of 13 -- 11 boys, 2 girls member of Lincoln Center Methodist Church
