1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=37217457
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Nov. 30, 1859 Union Salt Lake County Utah, USA Death: 	Apr. 11, 1946 Provo Utah County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT PROVO - Mrs. Frances Ann Richards Mower, 86, died early Thursday morning at the home of a daughter, Mrs. George W. Tucker, 360 East Sixth North St., of causes incident to age.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Union, Salt Lake County, Nov. 30, 1859, a daughter of Silas W. and Kesiah Brady Richards. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She received her early education in Union and Salt Lake.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Nov. 21, 1877, in St. George, Mrs. Mower was married to John Albert Mower who died in Fairview, June 30, 1894. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was again married to Henry Mower in Manti, May 24, 1904. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mower assisted in the rearing of Henry Mower's 11 children by a former marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in November, 1936, in Provo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mower moved from Fairview, Sanpete County, where she had resided for 50 years, to Provo in 1927. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was an active member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, having served as president of the primary in Fairview. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Daughters of the Utah Pioneers and of Provo Third Ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving Mrs. Mower are the following sons and daughters: Mrs. Keziah Tucker, Mrs. Cynthia Holliman and John F. Mower, Provo; Hyrum D. Mower, San Bernardino, Calif.; Jesse L. and Ernest E. Mower, Ogden; 50 grandchildren and 101 g
2 CONC reat grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Saturday at 11 a.m. in the Provo Third Ward Chapel under the direction of Bishop Arthur D. Taylor, and at 2:30 p.m. Saturday in the Fairview South Ward Chapel under direction of Bishop Howard W. Rigby
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call at the Quist Funeral Home in Provo Friday evening and at the George W. Tucker residence, 360 East Sixth North St., Saturday prior to services. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The casket will be opened briefly before the service in Fairview at 2:30 p.m. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment will be in the Fairview Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Deseret News April, 1946
