1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She is a daughter of Lindsay Anderson Brady, Jr. and Rebecca Emily (Pritchett) Brady.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary from SLC Tribune - Feb 1948 Fairview, Sanpete County, Feb 20.  Funeral services for Mrs. Nancy Rebecca Brady Miner, 73, who died in Salt Lake City Thursday , will be conducted Monday in Fairview South Ward chapel, Church 
2 CONC of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, by Otis Neilson, bishop. Burial will be in Fairview city cemetery.  Friends may call at the family residence Sunday evening and Monday prior to funeral. A daughter of L.A. and Rebecca Brady, s
2 CONC he was born Jan. 4,1875 in Fairview.  She was married to Orson A. Miner Nov. 19, 1894, in the Manti LDS temple. A Fairview resident almost all her life, she was active in the LDS church, serving as president of the Relief society 
2 CONC for three years and on the wefare program of the society.  She was a visiting teacher for almost 20 years.  Surviving are her husband, six sons and three daughters. O.L. Miner, Provo: M.C. Miner, Pomona, Cal.; A. L. Miner, Helper,
2 CONC  Carbon county;  Alma B. Miner, Mrs J. E. Black, Salt Lake City; Venoi Miner, Compton, Cal.; Mrs. R. S. Rasmussen, Monroe, Sevier county, Mrs J. R. Jensen and P. J. Miner, Fairview; 30 grandchildren and eight great-grandchildren. 
2 CONC Inscription: MINER
2 CONT  MOTHER NANCY R. 1875-1948
2 CONT  FATHER ORSON A. 1874-1949
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=27230193 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 17 2017, 12:08:19 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She is a daughter of Lindsay Anderson Brady, Jr. and Rebecca Emily (Pritchett) Brady.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary from SLC Tribune - Feb 1948
2 CONT Fairview, Sanpete County, Feb 20.
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Nancy Rebecca Brady Miner, 73, who died in Salt Lake City Thursday , will be conducted Monday in Fairview South Ward chapel, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, by Otis Neilson, bishop.
2 CONT Burial will be in Fairview city cemetery. Friends may call at the family residence Sunday evening and Monday prior to funeral.
2 CONT A daughter of L.A. and Rebecca Brady, she was born Jan. 4,1875 in Fairview. She was married to Orson A. Miner Nov. 19, 1894, in the Manti LDS temple.
2 CONT A Fairview resident almost all her life, she was active in the LDS church, serving as president of the Relief society for three years and on the wefare program of the society. She was a visiting teacher for almost 20 years.
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, six sons and three daughters. O.L. Miner, Provo: M.C. Miner, Pomona, Cal.; A. L. Miner, Helper, Carbon county; Alma B. Miner, Mrs J. E. Black, Salt Lake City; Venoi Miner, Compton, Cal.; Mrs. R. S. Rasmu
2 CONC ssen, Monroe, Sevier county, Mrs J. R. Jensen and P. J. Miner, Fairview; 30 grandchildren and eight great-grandchildren.
2 CONT Inscription
