1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Al Atkins, railroad and road contractor in Arizona for the last 21 years, died at the Nelson hospital in Mesa Tuesday afternoon at 3 o clock following a lingering illness. Mr. Atkins had been ill since early summer
2 CONC  and was operated on last week for tumor. The ailment was found to be cancer of the stomach however, and the affliction was so far advanced and in such condition that it was found by the physicians 1n charge impractical to operate
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was the son of William and Rachael Atkins of St. George, Utah, and spent his early life in that vicinity farming and raising stock. He came to Arizona 21 years ago and has been over much o! the state as a railroad and
2 CONC  road contractor, residing for a number o! years past in North Evergreen Acres near Mesa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Atkins was married to Mrs. Lottie Merrill, and surviving him are his wife and six children, all living here. A brother from St. George bas been here since the intended operation a week ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased has a wide circle of acqaintances over the state, who will regret to learn of his death. He has been road overseer in the Mesa district for the past year, and was a member of Damon Lodge, Knights of Phythias of Mesa.
