2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles Anderson Brady was reportedly born in about 1750 in King and Queen, Virginia, with his family origins from County Ulster, Ireland. His estate inventory is listed in the National Archives dated 28 Dec 1801. 
2 CONC He married Rebecca Catherine Good. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles' children, as far as we know are: William Anderson Brady (1773 - ) Thomas Anderson Brady (1774 - 1858) Charles Anderson Brady (1776 - ) Nancy Anderson Brady (1776 - ) Stephen Anderson Brady (1778 - 1833) William Anderson B
2 CONC rady (1780 - 1844) Martha Anderson Brady (1780 - ) Stephen Goldsby Brady (1783 - )
2 CONT
2 CONT There are records showing his participation in the Revolutionary War, being listed as a 3 Cl. on the Pay Roll of the January 1777, 3rd Virginia Regiment, led by Col. George Weedon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Records show a petition presented to the courts in Mercer County, Kentucky relieving him of paying personal levies and taxes due to his age and infirmities.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried in Gerard County, Kentucky.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=138539868 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 17 2017, 12:37:18 UTC''
