1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Sarah Ellen Thompson Wilson, 87, pioneer resident of this city. Mrs. Wilson died Friday at the home of a daughter, Mrs. A. H. Malben in Arthur, of causes incident to age.  She was the widow of James Wilson, an
2 CONC d for many years conducted a hotel here. Surviving are a son, Frank Pritchett of Richfield; two daughters, Mrs. Malben and Mrs. Floyd Anderson of Magna; a sister, Mrs. Amanda West of Pocatello, Idaho; eight grandchildren; seven gr
2 CONC eat-grandchildren and one great-great-grandchild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Salt Lake Tribune February 1, 1942
