3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Byron Francis Sheffield peacefully passed away just days before his 101st birthday on February 4, 2011 at his daughter's home in Anaheim, California. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Byron was born in a three- room house in Brigham City, Utah on February 15, 1910 to James and Dagmar Sheffield. He had one brother and three sisters. Byron worked in the family grocery stores, and following his LDS mission to Germ
2 CONC any, took over one of three family owned stores in Salt Lake. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was elected President of Salt Lake Butchers and Grocers Association. He managed this store until being overtaken by the incoming supermarkets. Byron then worked for Dan's Foods managing the drug store until his retirement in 19
2 CONC 75. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Byron married Arvella Exeter in 1931 just prior to leaving for his German mission. They had three children, son Byron Thomas, deceased, daughters Susanne and Joan. They were married for thirty-four years until Arvella's death in 1
2 CONC 965. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1969, he married June Marceil Williams. At the time of her death in 2005, Byron moved to California to live with his daughters, and be close to his grandchildren, and great-grandchildren. All of whom are so fortunate to have ha
2 CONC d him in their lives for so long. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Byron is survived by his daughters, seven grandchildren, ten great-grandchildren, sister, Beth Love, and nieces and nephews. Also survived by extended family three step-daughters (one deceased), one stepson, eight grandchildren, s
2 CONC ixteen great-grandchildren, and one great-great-granddaughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed golf in his retirement, and experienced three holes in one. Byron was a gentle man and loved by all who knew him. A festive memorial celebration was held on Byron's 100th birthday, which he enjoyed and was attended by m
2 CONC any family and friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside Services will be held at Larkin Sunset Lawn Mortuary and Cemetery, 2350 East 1300 South, Salt Lake City, on Tuesday, February 15, 2011 (his 101st birthday) at 12:00 p.m. A visitation will be held one hour prior to the se
2 CONC rvices at the same location. Published in the Deseret News on February 13, 2011.
