1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MESA -- Mrs. Nancy Elvira Cox Bench, 81, a resident of Mesa 22 years, died last night in the home of a daughter, Mrs. Ireta Updike, in Phoenix.  Mrs. Bench, born in Fairview, Utah, came to Mesa in 1942. She resided
2 CONC  at the home of a sister, Mrs. Belva Watson.  She was a member of the Alma Second Ward of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints.  Also surviving are another daughter, Mrs. Nora Cox of Boston; three sons, Walter Bench of 
2 CONC Las Vegas and Worth and Kirby Bench of Fairview; a brother, Frank Cox of Mesa; a brother and two sisters, all out of state; 25 grandchildren and two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be in at 5 p.m. tomorrow in Meldrum Mortuary.  Burial will be in Fairview.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arizona Republic, Wednesday March 18, 1964, transcribed by Rhonda Holton
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Walter Cox and Nancy Sanders
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: John Longman Bench Jr.
2 CONT
