2 CONT Deseret News 1886-03-17 death notices Page 16 OBITUARY MILLETT – In Kirksville, Washington County, Utah Territory, on the 16th of January 1886, of old age and debility, Sister Anna Millett, relict of the late Artemus Millett of Sc
2 CONC ipio Millard County and daughter of Joseph and Anna Stout, born in Madison County Tennessee Dec 22, 1806. She embraced the gospel in 1832 and shared the persecutions of the saints in Missouri and Illinois with unwavering fidelity 
2 CONC to the cause of truth. One instance might be mentioned illustrative of her pluck. When General Lucas sacked the town of Far West her step sons were taken among the prisoners, though of minor age. She in company with the wife of Br
2 CONC o Wm Allred whose sons were likewise held as prisoners rode into the camp though the jeers and curses of the mobocratic soldiery and proceeding to headquarters, demanded and obtained the release of their sons. She has ever lived t
2 CONC he life of a faithful Latter-day Saint and her nearest friends have never heard her breathe a doubt in regard to the promises of the Gospel covenant. Peace to her remains.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Deseret News 1886-03-17 death notices Page 16.OBITUARY: MILLETT – In Kirksville, Washington County, Utah Territory, on the 16th of January 1886, of old age and debility, Sister Anna Millett, relict of the late Artemus Millett of S
2 CONC cipio Millard County and daughter of Joseph and Anna Stout, born in Madison County Tennessee Dec 22, 1806. She embraced the gospel in 1832 and shared the persecutions of the saints in Missouri and Illinois with unwavering fidelity
2 CONC  to the cause of truth. One instance might be mentioned illustrative of her pluck. When General Lucas sacked the town of Far West her step sons were taken among the prisoners, though of minor age. She in company with the wife of B
2 CONC ro Wm Allred whose sons were likewise held as prisoners rode into the camp though the jeers and curses of the mobocratic soldiery and proceeding to headquarters, demanded and obtained the release of their sons. She has ever lived 
2 CONC the life of a faithful Latter-day Saint and her nearest friends have never heard her breathe a doubt in regard to the promises of the Gospel covenant. Peace to her remains.
2 CONT -------
2 CONT From the diary of Allen Joseph Stout (Anna's brother): I, [Allen Joseph Stout], The son of Joseph Stout, the son of Samuel Stout, the son of Peter Stout, was born in the county of Mercer and state of Kentucky, on the 5th day of De
2 CONC cember, A.D. 1815. My mother's name was Anna, the daughter of Daniel and Pleasant Smith. My grandmother Stout's name was Rachel Chauncey before she was married. My father, being a poor man, maintained his family by tending a grist
2 CONC mill. In the fall of 1819 he removed to Clinton County, Ohio, and there maintained his family partly by farming and partly by days work. In the summer of 1823, my father sent me to Rebecca Stout, a cousin of mine, 20 days. This, w
2 CONC ith the former exertions of my mother, enabl to begin to read. In the summer of 1823, my youngest sister Elizabeth Mahala died of the measles; I also had the same complaint, and about the same year I had the French measles of chic
2 CONC ken pox, and the mumps, and now whooping cough. On the 29th day of July, 1824, my mother died of the consumption after a long confinement and much suffering. She left a family of eight children whose names were: Rebecca, Sarah, Ma
2 CONC ry, Margaret, Anna, Hosea, Allen J. and Lydia R.
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Anna married Benjamin Jones
2 CONT Tazewell County Illinois marriage Records Index 1827-1859 compiled by David C. Perkins; published and copyrighted by Tazewell County Genealogical Society Box 312 Pekin, Illinois 61554. Anna Stout and Benjamin Jones [a widower] wer
2 CONC e married 29 Nov 1832. [found by Helen Willden]
2 CONT
2 CONT List of Members of Rich Branch Area on Log Creek: Benjamin Jones. A widower, Jones later married Anna Stout (sister of Hosea)…the wedding was performed by Rich in Illinois [Arrington, p. 22]. Jones entered two 40 acre parcels in (
2 CONC Rockford) Township 55, Range 29. The first was 2/26/37 being the NE ¼ of SW ¼ Sec. 11 and the other was done two months later SW ¼ of NE ¼ of Sec. 10. http://www.farwesthistory.com/rbranch2.htm  When Joseph and son Allen returned 
2 CONC to Taswell County in the spring of 1837 Anna had married a man by the name of Benjamin Jones, a Mormon...[from a Stout website that is no longer valid-by unknown author] "On the 5th of July, 1837, father and I set out for Caldwell
2 CONC  County, Missouri, in company with Anna and Jones family, and what was called the Rich branch of the Church. C.[Charles] C. Rich was our leader." {journal of Allen Joseph Stout]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes from Helen Willden:
2 CONT Before Hosea and Allen Joseph joined the church Anna joined first. Hosea states in his journal that Anna married a Mormon widow who had 5 children. The father of the five children was Ben Jones. Later divorced-- about 1848
2 CONT
2 CONT From the diary of her brother, Hosea Stout:
2 CONT Thursday July 8th 1847... Today Anna Jones my sister came here to live as her and her husband Ben Jones had parted for some of the dissatisfaction between them.
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Family records state that she married Moses Martin Sanders 24 Jan 1852 in the Endowment House in Salt Lake City. The early church records of Moses Martin Sanders does not list Anna as being married to him. The dates are found on t
2 CONC he IGI.
2 CONT ------
2 CONT From the Journal of Hosea Stout:
2 CONT Thursday 25 Nov 1858. I forgot to mention that on yesterday Anna was married to Artemus Millett. Started home with him to San Pete Co. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note by Juanita Brooks in On the Mormon Frontier page 669: footnote 37: Stout's sister, Anna was married to Benjamin Jones, a widower, with five children, in 1832, and had been granted a divorce by Brigham Young in February 1850. 
2 CONC She had no children of her own.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/41471/anna-millett Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 31 2022, 21:34:43 UTC''
2 CONT
