1 NAME Daniel /Odell/
2 GIVN Daniel
2 SURN Odell
2 _MARNM Odell
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Thomas Cemetery -Smith's Cove
2 ADDR
3 CITY Digby
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canada
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1733
2 ADDR
3 CITY Beekman
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 DEC 1816
2 ADDR
3 CITY Smiths Cove
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canaga
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A loyalist (to British rule), went to Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. The Hereditary Order of the Descendants of The Loyalists and Patriots of The American Revolution #308
2 CONT
2 CONT The Settlers of the Beekman Patent, p. 616
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	1733 Westerly Washington County Rhode Island, USA Death: 	Dec. 6, 1816 Digby Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Odle dit Daniel Odell Sr. and his family lived in Beekman, Dutchess County, New York Provience prior to the Revolutionary War. He married Mary Spalding about 1753 in Dutchess County, Provience of New York, British Colonial 
2 CONC America, a union that produced five children: Uriah (b. 1755); Phebe (b. 1758); Abijah (b. 1758); Daniel Jr. (b. 1760); and Mary (b. 1764). Daniel was a "loyalist", one who did not agree with the colonial independence movement wan
2 CONC ting to remain loyal to the British Crown. All Daniel's personal and real property were confiscated by New York State during the Revolutionary War. Daniel removed to Nova Scotia, Canada around the time of the British surrender in 
2 CONC 1783, being one of perhaps more than 50,000 American Colonists who remained loyal British Subjects and removed to Canada. Daniel and Mary lived in the Digby Nova Scotia area for the remainder of their lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, Daniel's possible first wife Mary Spalding Odle evidently died unexpectedly sometime shortly after 1784 probably in Nova Scotia, Canada. Daniel then married his beloved second wife Elizabeth Hunt, 7 Dec 1787 probabl
2 CONC y in Digby, Nova Scotia. Elizabeth and Daniel started a new family bringing eight children into the world. Elizabeth survived Daniel for over a decade, passing away in Canada about 1830. This contributor will leave it to others wi
2 CONC th direct blood relationship to enter a Find-A-Grave profile for Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: "The Settlers of the Beekman Patent, Dutchess County, New York." Volume IX, by Frank J. Doherty. Copyright 2007. pp. 616-620. Daniel Odell was probably the Private Daniel Odle, who served in the Revolutionary War Southe
2 CONC rn Campaign under loyalist Captain Andrew Maxwell, in General Montfort Brown's Prince of Wales Regiment. If true, Daniel was a combatant loyalist who actively fought for King and Crown against the rebel Patriots…and this is why Da
2 CONC niel had to move to Nova Scotia, Canada following the British defeat in 1783. **
2 CONT
2 CONT **Relevant work cited in this reference: "Loyalists in the Southern Campaign of the Revolutionary War, Volume III: Official Rolls of Loyalists Recruited from the Middle Atlantic Colonies, with Lists of Refugees from Other Colonies
2 CONC ." Copyright 1999. by Murtie June Clark. pp. 249-253.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 249: Muster rolls, Captain Andrew Maxwell's Company, Prince of Wales American Regiment, commanded by Brigadier General Montfort Brown, Charlestown, SC, 24 Feb 1781 to 24 Apr 1781, line # 21, shows Private Daniel Odle "on comman
2 CONC d" for 60 days inclusive.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 250: Muster rolls, Captain Andrew Maxwell's Company, Prince of Wales American Regiment, commanded by Brigadier General Montfort Brown, Charlestown, SC, 25 Apr 1781 to 24 Jun 1781, line # 21, shows Private Daniel Odle "on comman
2 CONC d" for 61 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 251: Muster rolls, Captain Andrew Maxwell's Company, Prince of Wales American Regiment, commanded by Brigadier General Montfort Brown, Beaufort, SC, 25 Oct 1781 to 24 Dec 1781, line # 21, shows Private Daniel Odle present 61 da
2 CONC ys.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 252: Muster rolls, Captain Andrew Maxwell's Company, Prince of Wales American Regiment, commanded by Brigadier General Montfort Brown, James Island, SC, 25 Apr 1782 to 24 Jun 1782, line # 21, shows Private Daniel Odle present 6
2 CONC 1 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 253: Muster rolls, Captain Andrew Maxwell's Company, Prince of Wales American Regiment, commanded by Brigadier General Montfort Brown, Long Island, 25 Dec 1782 to 24 Feb 1783, line # 16, shows Private Daniel Odle present 61 day
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Mary Valentine Spalding Odle dit Odell (1735 - 1785)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Uriah Odel (1755 - 1834)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Thomas Cemetery Digby Digby County Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: DJ Paul Record added: Jan 14, 2013 Find A Grave Memorial# 103583864
