1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Thomas Cadwell, III''' was the son of '''Hannah Butler''' and '''Lieutenant Thomas Cadwell'''.  Thomas was their first child and married '''Hannah Francis''', a daughter of Mercy Chatterton and John Francis.
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in West Hartford. About 1736 they were among those who petitioned the General Assembly for "parish priviledges", which would create a new church parish for residents of portions of Windsor, Farmington and Simsbury, thus
2 CONC  establishing a new parish called, after the names of the three towns, Win-ton-bury.  This area also included a portion of West Hartford, and was the parish of several generations of Cadwells.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Hannah had seven children: Thomas, md. Mary Porter; Abigail, md. Israel Merrill; Matthew, md. Elizabeth Hubbard; Hannah, md. John Hubbard, Jr.; Mary, md. Nathaniel Hubbard; Anne, md. Peletiah Pierce and Lois, md. Ashbel
2 CONC l Humphrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas made his will September 1747 and amended it two years later. Thanks for finding his death date go to RAMONA MIZNE - Thank you!
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-401763-1-754/thomas-cadwell-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-02e598081e359c725ce890c9097957b2&mrid=a484c91170507f887ce462bd610ff842 MyHeritage Family Tr
2 CONC ees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 4 2016, 7:24:21 UTC''
