1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Merrill-892
2 CONT Moses Merrill (1702 - 1776)
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Merrill aka Merrells
2 CONT Born 25 Dec 1702 in Hartford, Connecticutmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Daniel Merrill and Susanna (Pratt) Merrill
2 CONT Brother of Daniel Merrill, Susanna (Merrill) Steele, Jonathan Merrill, Ruth Merrill, Mary Merrill, Hepzibah (Merrill) Seymour, Daniel Merrill, Israel Merrill, Mary Merrill, Hezekiah Merrill and Rachel (Merrill) Shepard
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Cook) Merrill — married 1726 in East Hartford, Hartford, Connecticutmap
2 CONT Husband of Rachel (Wells) Merrill — married 20 Nov 1740 [location unknown]
2 CONT Husband of Bathsheba (Pettibone) Merrill — married 12 Jan 1766 in Farmington, Ct., recorded at West Hartford. Ct.map
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Ruth (Merrill) Adams, Lodema (Merrill) Goodwin, Moses Merrill, Rachel (Merrill) Porter and Eleazor Merrill
2 CONT Died 4 Aug 1776 at age 73 in Farmington, Hartford, Connecticutmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Eric Johnson private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 14 Dec 2023 | Created 30 Apr 2012
2 CONT This page has been accessed 601 times.
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT 1 Biography
2 CONT 1.1 Children
2 CONT 1.2 Research Notes
2 CONT 2 Sources
2 CONT 2.1 See also
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 December 1702 born in Hartford, Connecticut, to Daniel and Susannah (Pratt) Merrill[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1) Mary Cooke, b. 2 June 1706, daughter of Aaron Cooke and Martha Alleyn.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (2) 20 November 1740 Rachel Wells, bp. 20 January 1716/7, d. 31 October 1763, daughter of Samuel Wells and Rachel Cadwell.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (3) 12 January 1766 Bathsheba Grimes of Simsbury[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 August 1776 died in West Hartford[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Bathsheba was married shortly thereafter to Moses Merrills, who then died within a year, before the tax list was prepared in 1778, when she was described as his widow."[4][5]
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Moses and Mary (Cooke) Merrill:[2]
2 CONT Ruth, bp. 28 May 1727, m. Ebenezer Adams
2 CONT Laodamia, b. 28 January 1728/9, m. Samuel Goodwin
2 CONT Moses, bp. 18 July 1731, m. (1) Waitstill Heath, (2) Elizabeth Wells
2 CONT Children of Moses and Rachel (Wells) Merrill:[2]
2 CONT Mary, bp. 26 July 1741, m. Seth Barker
2 CONT Samuel, bp. 2 March 1755, d. 2 September 1772
2 CONT Rachel, m. Noah Porter
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT 'I tracked down the details on the third marriage. It does not appear in any of the relevant vital or church records. The date that has been bouncing around the internet, and which I passed to you, is not of their marriage itself.
2 CONC  On 12 Jan. 1766 at the West Hartford church, Moses Merril of Farmington and Bathsheba Grimes of Symsbury, published their intention to marry, but their marriage itself does not appear in the records of that church. It must have h
2 CONC appened by 15 June 1766, when Bathsheba, wife of Moses Merril, was admitted to the church fellowship. The same West Hartford church records show Moses Merrills to have died 4 Aug. 1776 of "a complication of disorders", aged 70.'[5
2 CONC ]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Whittelsey, Charles B. The Ancestry and the Descendants of John Pratt of Hartford, Conn. Hartford, CT: The Case, Lockwood & Brainard Company, 1900. Page 19.
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 2.2 2.3 2.4 2.5 2.6 Barbour, Lucius Barnes. Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut. Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1977. Page 397.
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch ([1] : 7 January 2020), Daniell Merrill in entry for Moses Merrill, 1702.
2 CONT ↑ Petttibone Register, p 70.
2 CONT ↑ 5.0 5.1 Personal Communication from Todd Farmerie, Entered by Tom Bredehoft, 7/8/2013
2 CONT See also
2 CONT
