2 CONT 79. MOSES9 MERRILL (DANIEL8, JOHN7 *MERRILL, NATHANIEL6, NATHANIEL5, JOHN4 *MERRELL, THE YOUNGER, JOHN3 *MERYELL, JOHN2, THOMAS1) was born December 25, 1702 in Hartford, Hartford, Conn, and died August 4, 1776 in West Hartford, Ha
2 CONC rtford, Conn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT *(1) SARAH COOK Bef. 1727. She was born June 2, 1706 in Hartford, Hartford, Conn, and died 1740. 
2 CONT *(2) RACHEL WELLES November 20, 1740 in West Hartford, CT, daughter of SAMUEL WELLES and RACHEL CADWELL. She was born Bef. January 20, 1711/12 in Hartford, Hartford, Conn, and died October 31, 1763 in New Hartford, Litchfield, Con
2 CONC n. 
2 CONT *(3) BATHSHEBA GRIMES January 12, 1766 in Farmington, CT. She was born Aft. 1740 in Simsbury, Conn, and died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for MOSES MERRILL: From "A Merrill Memorial" by Samuel Merrill, Cambridge, MA 1917-1928
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses(4) Merrill (Daniel(3), John(2)) was born 25 Dec 1702 in Hartford, CT and died 4 Aug 1776. He lived in West Hartford, and after 1755 in Farmington, CT. He married (1) in West Hartford, Sarah Cook; (2) 20 Nov 1740, Rachel ??, 
2 CONC who died 31 Oct 1765 in Westhartford, aet, 48, and (3) (published 12 Jan 1766, in West Hartford) Bathsheba Grimes (or Graham) of Simsbury. *
2 CONT
2 CONT * it has been queried whether this third marriage was not instead the first marrigae of Moses, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of MOSES MERRILL and SARAH COOK are: 
2 CONT *i. RUTH10 MERRILL, b. Bef. May 28, 1727, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn. 
2 CONT *ii. LAODAMIA MERRILL, b. January 28, 1728/29, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. May 6, 1790, Hartford, Hartford, Conn; m. SAMUEL GOODWIN, Abt. January 1749/50, Hartford, Hartford, Conn; b. October 10, 1710, Hartford, Hartford, Co
2 CONC nn; d. September 30, 1776, Hartford, Hartford, Conn. 
2 CONT *iii. MOSES MERRILL, b. Bef. July 18, 1731, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. April 3, 1794, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; m. (1) ELIZABETH WELLES, Abt. 1755, Hartford, hartford, Conn; b. Bef. September 2, 1722, Hartford, Hartfor
2 CONC d, Conn; d. September 15, 1772, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; m. (2) WAITSTILL HEATH, September 5, 1773, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; b. 1744, Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. February 19, 1826. 
2 CONT *iv. ALLEN MERRILL, b. 1734, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. July 11, 1771, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; m. MARY ANDRUS, May 4, 1766, Farmington, Conn; b. Abt. 1734; d. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of MOSES MERRILL and RACHEL WELLES are: 
2 CONT *v. MARY10 MERRILL, b. Bef. July 26, 1741, West Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. Unknown; m. SETH BARKER, April 15, 1764, Hartford, Hartford, Conn; b. Abt. 1740; d. Unknown. 
2 CONT *vi. SAMUEL MERRILL, b. Abt. 1743, Hartford, Hartford, Conn; d. September 2, 1772, Farmington, Conn. 
2 CONT *vii. ELEAZAR MERRILL, b. Abt. 1745; d. May 16, 1769; m. LOIS FOOTE, May 29, 1765, Farmington, Conn; b. April 4, 1746, Farmington, Conn; d. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of MOSES MERRILL and BATHSHEBA GRIMES is: 
2 CONT *viii. RACHEL10 MERRILL, b. 1766, Conn.; d. Unknown; m. NOAH PORTER, Abt. 1785; b. Bef. 1766, Conn.; d. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for RACHEL MERRILL: From "A Merrill Memorial" by Samuel Merrill, Cambridge, MA 1917-1928
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel (Merrill) Porter had three sons, Robert, Edward and Noah, and a daughter Sophia. the sons were all clergymen. The youngest, Rev. Noah Porter, D. D., was for more than sixty years pastor of the church in Farmington. At his h
2 CONC ouse was held, Sep 10 1810, the first meeting of the American Board of Copmmissioners ofr Foreign Missions. His son Ref. Dr. Noah Porter was President of Yale College 1871-86. Sophia Porter married Rev. Heman Humphrey, D. D., Pres
2 CONC ident of Amherst College 1823-45.
