1 OCCU Married Elmer F. Stewart September 23, 1908, in Bannock, Idaho;  they had 1 son, Clifford, in 1910.  Helper in a restaurant in Pocatello, Idaho, in 1910;  Married Fintis L. Leeper in Lincoln, Idaho, January 16, 1912, and had 2 mor
2 CONC e children
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth "Bessie" Hargraves was born May 20, 1891, in Pocatello, Bannock County, Idaho, to Samuel Hargraves and Mary Emily Merrill.  In the 1900 U.S. Federal Census for Bancroft, Bannock County, Idaho, they were l
2 CONC isted in the census record as follows:  Samuel, 35, Mary E., 33, Eliza J., 14, Elizabeth, 9, Agnes, 5, Lewis A., 3, Enoch Trane, 2, and also living in their home was Christian Mortensen, 23, listed as a boarder.  Samuel and Mary E
2 CONC mily had been married for 15 years, had given birth to 6 children, 5 of whom were still living.  Samuel was working as a farmer.  He was born in Utah, his father in Scotland and his mother in England.  Mary Emily was born in Idaho
2 CONC , her father in New York, and her mother in Utah.  All of their children were born in Idaho.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bessie married Elmer Frederick Stewart in Bannock, Idaho, in 1908 at the age of 17 years old.  However, In the 1910 U.S. Federal Census for Pocatello, Bessie Stewart, 19, was living with her 9-month old son, Clifford Stewart, and 
2 CONC her parents, Samuel, 41, and Emily Hargraves, 36, and her two brothers, Louis, 13, and Enoch Trane Hargraves, 11.  She had been married for two years, but her husband was not living with her family at the time for some reason.  He
2 CONC r father was working as a house carpenter, her mother as a dressmaker, and Bessie as a helper in a restaurant.  Also living in their home were two lodgers, Mr. J.B. Ripliner, 49, and Miss Frances McNally, 27.  Mr. Ripliner was fro
2 CONC m France and Miss McNally was born in Idaho, but her parents were both born in Ireland,  Mr. Ripliner had been married for 22 years, but his wife was not living with him for some reason.  Miss McNally  was single.  Mr. Ripliner wa
2 CONC s working as a tailor and Frances as a laborer in a yarn works.
2 CONT
2 CONT I don't know if Bessie's husband, Elmer Stewart, died or if they were divorced, but two years later she married Fintis L. Leeper, on January 16, 1912, in Lincoln County, Idaho, and by the 1920 census they were living on Utah Stree
2 CONC t in Gooding, Idaho, and were listed as follows in the census:  Fintis, 27, Bessie, 27, Clifford M. Leeper, 10, and Bert Leeper, 6.  Bessie's new husband, Fintis, must have adopted her son, Clifford Stewart, since Clifford is list
2 CONC ed as Clifford Leeper in this census record.  Clifford and his father had both been born in Idaho.  Fintis and his parents were born in Texas  He was working as a general laborer in a warehouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the 1930 census, the Leeper's were living in Eden, Jerome County, Idaho, and were listed as follows:  Fintis, 42, Bessie, 42, Bert, 15, and Ruth, 9 years old, but Clifford was no longer living with the family.  I did not find h
2 CONC im in a 1930 census record either, but at some point he moved to California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clifford Leeper was listed in the 1940 U.S. Federal Census living at 6524 Lucille Avenue in San Antonio, Los Angeles County, California, with his wife, Ruth.  He was 30 years old and she was 27.  Clifford was born in Idaho and Rut
2 CONC h in Nebraska.  In 1935 they had been living in Maywood, California.  He was working as a machinist with his own typewriter repair shop, and Ruth was working as a power machine operator in a mattress factory.  For the 52 weeks she
2 CONC  worked at that job at 40 hours per week in 1939 her income was $936.  Clifford did not disclose his income in the census record.  I'm not sure if they ever had any children or where they lived after 1940.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clifford Merrill Stewart Leeper, born August 8, 1910, passed away at the age of 54 years old on January 2, 1965, and was buried in the Fort Rosecrans National Cemetery in San Diego, California.  He had served in the U.S. Army as a
2 CONC  T-5 during World War II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bessie passed away November 26, 1980, and had been living in San Diego at the time of her death.
