1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David Lutz Emery, 84, passed away Tuesday, April 25, 1995.  He was born August 27, 1910, in Rexburg, Idaho, a son of George Henry and Effie Lodema Lutz Emry.  He married Zelda Hess March 25, 1933m in Salt Lake City
2 CONC , Utah. Their marriage was later solemnized in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.  He had lived in Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, California, Layton and in Kaysville for the past 22 years.  He retired from Mountain Fuel where he worked as a 
2 CONC serviceman.  He was an active member of the LDS Church, served as a counselor in the bishopric in Layton, Scout Master, Seventy, Sunday School superintendency, High priest Group leadership and home teacher. Filled five stake missi
2 CONC ons and was an extraction worker.  He enjoyed playing golf, music and playing the harmonica, gardening and spending time with his grandchildren and great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife of Kaysville; two sons and two daughters, Val D. Emery (Betty), Houston, Texas; Henry "Hank" Emery (Lana), Kaysville; Marjorie Emery Bell (Lee), South Weber; Joy Lynn Emery Twibey (George), Layton; 19 grandc
2 CONC hildren; 37 great-grandchildren. Also surviving are two brothers and two sisters, George R. Emery, Mesa, Arizona; Thomas Lutz Emery, Salt Lake City; Jessie Hatch, Boise, Idaho; and Ruth Moss (twin sister), Bountiful.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Saturday, April 29, 1995, 11 a.m., at the Mutton Hollow LDS Ward chapel, 855 East Mutton Hollow Road, Kaysville. Friends may call Friday, from 6-8 p.m. at Lindquist's Kaysville Mortuary, 400 North Mai
2 CONC n, and at the church Saturday, from 9:30-10:45 a.m. Interment, Kaysville City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Deseret News
