1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ruth Lutz Emery was one of eleven children born to George Henry Emery and Effie Lodema Lutz.  She and her twin brother David L. Emery were born at Rexburg, Idaho on August 27, 1910.  Her young life was full of hard
2 CONC ship.  Her father died when she was only seven, leaving her mother struggling to raise the family.  Ruth married Delbert Moss of Woods Cross in 1926 and they eventually settled in Bountiful near Five Points.  He died in 1971.  Her
2 CONC  twin brother David preceded her in death by exactly one year.  Her health has been deteriorating for several years.  She left this mortal life on 26 April at the Park View Nursing Home in Bountiful. Her family will miss her, but 
2 CONC we know that she is happier on the other side.  She will be remembered by her friends as someone who makes friends easily, outgoing and warm; and remembered by her family as a loyal, loving mother and a great cook.  Ruth is surviv
2 CONC ed by her children: Donald Moss of Farmington; Ralph Moss of Bountiful; Joyce Petersen of Woods Cross; Mickey K. Moss of Seattle; and Linda Jarman of Mount Pleasant.  She is also survived by brothers: George Emery of Arizona; Thom
2 CONC as Emery of Salt Lake; and sister, Jessie Hatch of Boise.  She leaves 18 grandchildren, 53 great-grandchildren and five great-great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Tuesday, April 30, 1996 at 12:00 noon at the Russon Brothers Bountiful Funeral Home, 295 North Main where friends may call Monday evening from 7:00 - 8:00 p.m. and Tuesday one hour prior to the servic
2 CONC es. Interment in the Bountiful City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Deseret News
