1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don Lutz Anderson, age 81, died December 19, 1992 at his home in Salt Lake City, Utah.  He was born June 9, 1911, in Rexburg, Idaho, to Byron Morley and Eleanore Roseltha Lutz Anderson.  Don married Vernell Christe
2 CONC nsen on January 2, 1934, in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.  He was the owner and operator of Don Anderson Signs for 38 years, was active in the LDS Church, and a member of South Cottonwood 4th Ward.  He served as High Priest group lead
2 CONC er and in stake Sunday School presidency.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by wife; four sons, Lee and wife, Karen, Salt Lake; Craig and wife, Ruth, Highland, Utah; Jeffrey and wife, Carlette, San Diego, California; Steve and wife, Susan, Tucson, Ariziona; daughter, Karen and husband, Jerry Mitc
2 CONC hell, Salt Lake; 14 grandchildren and 12 great-grandchildren; two brothers, DeWayne and wife, Nancy, Salt Lake; Rulon and wife, Mary Lou Anderson, South Carolina; three sisters, Andrea and husband, Reuben Whitney, Salt Lake; Mitz 
2 CONC Needham, Salt Lake; and Betty and husband, Jim Davidson, Oregon.  Preceded in death by parents, four sisters, and two brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services Tuesday, December 22nd, at 12 noon, South Cottonwood 4th Ward Chapel, 981 East 5600 South Street where friends may call Tuesday, 10 - 11:45 am. Burial, Larkin Sunset Gardens, 10600 South 1700 East.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published 20 December 1992 in The Salt Lake Tribune (UT)
2 CONT
2 CONT
