1 NOTE {geni:about_me} FUNERAL HELD FOR ARIZONA PIONEER:  Prescott, October 10, 1941:  Henry Augustus Martineau, one of the early Arizona Morman settlers and former Latter Day Saints church bishop at Concho, Arizona died last night at th
2 CONC e Arizona Pioneers home.  The pioneer settled in St Johns in 1879 after coming to Arizona from Utah, where he was born in 1852.  He entered the Pioneers' home in 1930.  Martineau leaves six children. Mrs Ida Jesperson and Howard M
2 CONC artineau, both of Binghampton, Arizona;  Mrs Bertha Farnsworth, Mesa;  Frank Martineau, Huntington Park, California;  Charles Martineau, Colonia Juarez, Mexico, and Mrs Adele Whetten, Colonia, Chihuahua, Mexico, and a sister, Mrs 
2 CONC Elvira Johnson, Prescott.  Funeral services were held this afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tucson Daily Citizen, October, 11, 1941.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional information provided by Don Stowell
2 CONT
