1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vinton Miller Merrill, beloved son, husband, father, grandfather and great-grandfather, passed away Thurs., August 12, 2004 in Bountiful, Utah. Born in Preston, Idaho to Leslie Vinton and Marie Miller Merrill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Afton Wilcox April 15, 1938 in the Logan LDS Temple. They were married 61 years.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended college at University of Utah, Brigham Young University and graduated from Utah State University. He received his Doctor of Medical Dentistry from North Pacific School of Dentistry in Portland, Oregon. He practiced den
2 CONC tistry in San Diego and Long Beach, California for 40 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vinton had a long history of service in the LDS Church, serving as Bishop of the Long Beach, California 8th Ward, Stake Presidency, Long Beach, California East Stake, Area Athletic Director for California, Arizona, and Nevada, Tem
2 CONC ple Worker in the Los Angeles Temple, Temple Worker Coordinator for temple missionaries in Salt Lake City, Utah. He served in the Berlin, Germany mission from 1934 - 1937. He and Afton served a temple mission to the Swiss Temple i
2 CONC n Bern, Switzerland from 1985 - 1987. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by his children, V. Brent Merrill (Terry) of Farmington, Utah, Tamara Collins (Alan) of Bountiful, Utah, Shanon Sommer (Ron) of Claremont, California, and Deborah Clark (R. Rand) of Tulsa, Oklahoma; brothers and sisters, 
2 CONC Venus Wheeler (Herbert), Carmen Dibble (Ralph, deceased), Gwen Reading (Roland), Douglas Merrill (Oksan) and Reed Merrill (Joan); 22 grandchildren and 30 great-grandchildren. Preceded in death by his wife, Afton; granddaughter, Me
2 CONC redith; and brother, Richard Merrill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services held Monday, August, 16, 2004 at the Bountiful Central Stake Center, 450 South 750 East, Bountiful. Interment – Smithfield City Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Salt Lake Tribune on 8/14/2004.
