1 OCCU Magnificent wife and mother
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of Leslie Vinton Merrill and Marie Rebecca Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT Married George Ralph Dibble, 26 Jun 1940, Logan, Cache, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary - Carmen Merrill Dibble, 86, died at her home in Layton, Utah Friday, October 27, 2006. She was born March 3, 1920, in Rexburg, Idaho; daughter of Leslie Vinton and Marie Rebecca Miller Merrill. A sweet, humble, obedient 
2 CONC daughter of God; she was reared in Idaho by wonderful, loving parents. 
2 CONT
2 CONT While attending the Utah State Agricultural College, she met and married George Ralph Dibble. They were married in the Logan Temple June 26, 1940. She came home then, to the family farm in West Layton, and became the best farm wif
2 CONC e and mother ever. She loved and served her family and her neighbors. She taught her children to pray, to sing, to work, and to love the Lord. She played the violin in a most beautiful, warm, melodic, expressive way, and served ma
2 CONC ny friends by playing the violin at their funerals. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She served in many capacities in church and community, including serving on the LDS Primary General Board from 1970-75. She also served with her husband in the Ogden LDS temple, and then together with him on a mission in the Londo
2 CONC n LDS Temple, from 1983-85. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her children, Ann (Mrs. Henry Dee Call) Bountiful, UT; Marie (Mrs. Willis F. McComas) Kaysville, UT; Cleve M. Dibble (Barbara) Layton, UT; Kent M. Dibble (Barbara Jean) Tempe, AZ; Jane (Mrs. James F. Hales) Fruit Hei
2 CONC ghts, UT; Ruth (Mrs. Kirk V. Bourne) Highland, UT; and Ellen (Mrs. Tyler J. Cox) Layton, UT; 34 grandchildren and 41 great-grandchildren; brothers and sisters, Venus (Mrs. J. Herbert Wheeler) St. George, UT; Gwen (Mrs. Roland G. R
2 CONC eading) Bend, OR; Douglas M. Merrill (Ok Sun) Layton, UT; Reed M. Merrill (Joan) River Heights UT; Ben T. Dibble, Scottsdale, AZ; Cleo B. Dibble, Washington D.C. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceding her in death were her husband, George Ralph Dibble; parents, brothers, Richard M. Merrill and Vinton M. Merrill; her first child, Celia; son-in-law, Brett F. Wood; and great-granddaughter, Emma Kristen Satchwell; brother
2 CONC s and sisters-in-law, Charles E. Dibble, Philo T. Dibble, Jane Dibble Farrer and Ruth T. Dibble. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service will be held Thursday, November 2, 2006 at 11 a.m. at the West Gentile LDS Chapel, 2120 West Gentile. Friends and family may call Wednesday, from 6-8 p.m. at the Lindquist's Layton Mortuary, 1867 North Fairfield Ro
2 CONC ad and Thursday from 9:30-10:30 a.m. at the chapel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment, Kaysville City Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As a family we wish to thank the many angels who have helped us care for Mother during the past four years.
