1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Douglas Miller Merrill (September 18, 1926 - May 16, 2013) U.S. Veteran
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Miller Merrill, 86, passed away Thursday, May 16, 2013.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born September 18, 1926 in Rexburg, Idaho the son of Leslie Vinton and Marie Merrill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas served in the Army, Coast Guard and U.S. Air Force.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Cresente Rose Pantazes on September 2, 1951 in Denver, Colorado. They were later divorced. He married Ok Sun Crowe on April 1, 2003 in Farmington, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas spent his life in the service of others. Of his many talents he was a gifted writer with an uncompromised memory. He was a loving father and husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife Ok Sun, Clearfield; sons, Richard Merrill, Salt Lake City; Leslie Merrill, Bountiful; William Merrill, Tomball, Texas; Shawn Crowe, Montgomery, Alabama; daughter Linda Erickson, Madeira Beach, Florida; broth
2 CONC er, Reed Miller Merrill, Logan; and sister, Gwen (Merrill) Reading, Bend, Oregon; along with 14 grandchildren and 6 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded in death by his parents, brothers, Vinton Miller Merrill, Richard M. Merrill, sisters, Venus Wheeler, and Carmen Dibble.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Monday, May 20, 2013 at 11 a.m. at Lindquist's Layton Mortuary, 1867 No. Fairfield Road. Friends may visit family Monday from 9:45 to 10:45 a.m. at the mortuary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment, Utah Veterans Memorial Park.
