1 NOTE {geni:about_me} VIVIAN ROMBOUGH, 1925 - 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT It is with the deepest sadness that we announce the passing of our mother, grandmother and great grandmother, Vivian Rombough (nee Collett) who passed away in Taber on Friday, December 2, 2011, at the age of 86 years with her daug
2 CONC hter and grandchildren at her side.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relatives and friends are invited to meet with the family in the Relief Society Room at the church prior to the funeral service on Wednesday, December 7, 2011 between 10:00 A.M. and 10:40 A.M.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Funeral Service will be held at The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, Taber Stake Centre, 4709 - 50 Avenue, Taber on Wednesday, December 7, 2011 at 11:00 A.M. with Bishop Wade Steed conducting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family burial to follow at the Taber Memorial Garden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vivian is survived by her children and grandchildren, her three sons and their children; daughter and her children. She is also survived by nineteen great grandchildren, her sister, her brother, five sisters-in-law, a brother-in-l
2 CONC aw as well as numerous nieces, nephews and close relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was predeceased by her son David Blair; husband Archie; parents Morgan and Phoebe Collett; mother and father-in-law Sam and Jean Rombough; brother Harold Collett; great grandchildren Bret, Brentson, Alisa Lehman and numerous o
2 CONC ther relations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vivian was born in Taber April 17, 1925, the eldest daughter of Morgan and Phoebe (nee Wilson) Collett and received her schooling in Taber.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Archie on February 19, 1944, and they were blessed with five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their early years were spent on the family farm south of Taber with a move into town after the death of their son Blair.  Archie predeceased Vivian September 20, 1978.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her last twenty six years were spent in long term care at the Taber Continuing Care and with the last few months at the Linden View facility.  We will treasure always the many care givers, volunteers and life long friends she made
2 CONC  during her stays in both facilities.
2 CONT
2 CONT If friends so desire, memorial tributes in Vivian's name may be made directly to the Taber Hospital Foundation (Long Term Care), 4326 - 50 Avenue, Taber, Alberta T1G 1N9 or to the Arthritis Society Alberta & NWT Division, 20, 1301
2 CONC  - 8 Street SW, Calgary, Alberta T2R 1B7.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgan Collett (1904 - 1975)
2 CONT
2 CONT Phoebe Wilson Collett (1905 - 1980)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT
2 CONT Archie Rombough (1921 - 1978)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Blair Rombough (1946 - 1956)
2 CONT
2 CONT Headstone Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT ROMBOUGH
2 CONT
2 CONT VIVIAN,17 APRIL 1925, 02 DEC. 2011 FOREVER IN OUR HEARTS
2 CONT
2 CONT ARCHIE, 24 MARCH 1921, 18 SEPT. 1978 GONE BUT NOT FORGOTTEN
2 CONT
