1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gordon Bruce Merrill was born February 4, 1930, to Arthur Bruce Merrill and his wife Helen.  Gordon was listed in the 1940 U.S. Federal Census for Maricopa County, Arizona, living on 18th Avenue and Indian School R
2 CONC oad, with his parents and sister.  They owned their home which was valued at $1,500 and they were listed as follows in the census record:  Bruce Merrill, 35, Helen, 30, Gordon, 10, and Barbara Jean, 6 years old.  They had been liv
2 CONC ing in Solomonville, Graham County, Arizona, in 1935.  Bruce had 4 years of high school education, Helen had 2 years, Gordon was in the 5th grade and his sister Barbara Jean was in the first grade.  They were all born in Arizona e
2 CONC xcept for Helen who was born in Texas.  Gordon's father was working as a salesman in a dry goods store, and for the 24 weeks he worked at that profession for 48 hours per week in 1939 his income was $500.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gordon was pictured in a 1947 North Phoenix High School Yearbook and was studying accounting.  He joined the U.S. Air Force on November 6, 1950, and was not released from service until April 30, 1973.  In a 1952 U.S. City Director
2 CONC y for Phoenix, Arizona, he was living with his parents at 2802 E. Elm Drive and was working for the U.S. Air Force.  He was listed again in a 1957 directory for Phoenix with his wife Patricia Kathleen Egan, and they were living at
2 CONC  4324 E. Palm Lane.  His parents Arthur and Helen were still living at 2802 E. Elm Drive. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gordon and his wife Patricia had been married October 3, 1953, in Bounemouth, England.  Gordon must have been stationed in England while serving in the Air Force when he married Patric.  Their first daughter, Karen Lee, was born i
2 CONC n England in October of 1954, and when she was 7 months old, the three of them arrived at Idlewild Airport in New York City, having flown from Burtonwood Air Force Base in England.  On the passenger manifest for their flight from 
2 CONC England to America, Gordon was listed as a Staff Sargent.  Their weights were listed as 170 pounds for Gordon, 130 pounds for Patricia and 20 pounds for their daughter, Karen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patricia Kathleen Egan Merrill petitioned for naturalization on December 11, 1958, in Phoenix, Arizona.  She was born April 26, 1935, in Bournemouth, England, and at the time of her application, was living in Apartment #308 in Wes
2 CONC tward Manor in Goodyear, Maricopa County.  She was 5'-8" tall and weighed 130 pounds and was listed as a housewife.  She indicated that she had two children, Karen Lee Merrill, born in Swindon, England, October 23, 1954, and Kelly
2 CONC  Lynn Merrill born June 13, 1957, probably in Phoenix, Arizona. She had arrived for permanent residence in the United States in New York City on June 12, 1955.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1993 Patricia K. Merrill was living at 9182 Firelight Way in Sacramento, California.  Gordon Bruce Merrill passed away December 18, 2006, while living in Sacramento, California.  I don't know if Patricia is still living, but if
2 CONC  so she would be about 82 years old today.
