1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints Church History website, Early Mormon Missionaries:   William Wesley Williams served an LDS Mission to the Southern States from December, 1896 to April of 1899.  
2 CONC He was 21 years old when he was called to go on the mission.  He was set apart December 9, 1896, and the end date was April 17, 1899.  He held the office of a Seventy in the Priesthood.  He was called from the Gentile Valley in Ba
2 CONC nnock County, Idaho, and was set apart by Jonathan G. Kimball.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://history.lds.org/missionary/individual/william-wesley-williams-1875?lang=eng
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the son of Robert Hanna Williams and Harriet Abigail Busenbark.  He married Emma Perry September 28, 1899, in Logan, Cache County, Utah.  She passed away in 1914.  He married Florence Claire Cranney November 24, 1915. 
2 CONC  He married Clarissa Cyrena "Chloe" (Merrill) Jolley November 16, 1949, in Mesa, Maricopa, Arizona.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
