1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wilma Hanks was the daughter of George Augustus Hanks and Melissa Jane Merrill.  Her mother died of typhoid fever when she was just one month old and she was raised by her maternal grandparents.  She did not see he
2 CONC r father again until she was 17 years old.  Wilma married Leland Theodore Seidel, August 12, 1933, in Franklin, Greenlee, Arizona.  The following is her Life History - Wilma Hanks Seidel as she told it herself:  I was born at That
2 CONC cher, Graham County, Arizona, and was only one month old when my mother took typhoid fever and died on December 13, 1901, leaving me with my grandmother and grandfather, Thomas Steven Merrill and Ester Ann Collett.  My father, Geo
2 CONC rge A. Hanks, went back to Utah and there married Bessie Bennets Johns, and I never saw my father until I was 17 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have always been taught the gospel and have tried to live it.  My young girlhood was spent at Franklin, Greenlee County, Arizona, and going to school at Neblet, New Mexico.  I have been president of Relief Society at Jerome Ariz
2 CONC ona, Branch of the California Mission, have taught in Sunday School, M. I. A. and Primary; have been president of Y. W. M. I A. of Kirtland ward for two years, had to be released in 1951 because of a car accident which took me a c
2 CONC ouple of years to overcome.  Have been secretary of Relief Society and at present am a visiting teacher, also magazine representative, also Instructor Representative for the Kirtland Ward - 1959. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
