1 OCCU Married Ira Donald Welker May 27, 1938.  Temple marriage was May 26, 1962.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Phyllis Welker was the daughter of Roy and Clara M. Tippets Merrill.  Phyllis married Ira Donald Welker on May 27, 1938.  Their Temple marriage was on May 26, 1962.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===OBITUARY FROM THE EASTERN ARIZONA COURIER, SAFFORD, ARIZONA, PUBLISHED ON WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 25, 2006:===
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Phyllis Welker were conducted Tuesday, January 10, at the 20th St. LDS Chapel in Safford with Bishop Lynn Smith officiating. Interment followed in the Safford Cemetery.  Phyllis Tippets Welker was born Jan. 4,
2 CONC  1920, in Hayden, the daughter of Roy and Tillie Merrill.  When she was a child, Phyllis' family moved to Mesa, where she grew up and attended school. Phyllis married Don Welker on May 27, 1938. Shortly thereafter, they moved to S
2 CONC afford to make their home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phyllis was a faithful member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, serving in the Safford Fifth Ward. She held many callings in the ward and stake level. Phyllis also served as a temple worker in the Mesa LDS Temple
2 CONC , work she thoroughly enjoyed. She was an avid seamstress, enjoyed singing, baking and fishing in the White Mountains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her children, Bob (Betty) Welker of Payson, Dian (Art) Moore of Safford, Joyce (Del) Johnson of Safford, Rick (Linda) Welker of Safford, and Dan (Louise) Welker of Thatcher; 30 grandchildren; 67 great-grandchildr
2 CONC en; and six great-great-grandchildren; brother, Ken Merrill; sisters, Ruth Carpenter and Nelda Adair. Phyllis was preceded in death by her sweetheart, Don Welker; two brothers and two sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements for Phyllis Welker were entrusted to Bunker's Caldwell Chapel.
2 CONT
