1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abigail married Obadiah King II on September 24, 1782. They had 14 children: Rachel L., David D., Lewis, Charlotte, Josiah, Rebecca, Samuel, Abigail, Obadiah III, Betsey, Polly, Joshua, Jacob and Sally.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''NOTE''': Abigail was supposedly born in Frederick, Dutchess County. However, Frederick did not exist as of 1764. As of 1740 the South Precinct of Dutchess County became known as the Fredericksburgh Precinct. Its name was chan
2 CONC ged to Frederickstown in March 1788. In 1795, the name Frederickstown was changed to the Town of Frederick, See https://livingplaces.com/ny/putnam_county.html
2 CONT * Abigail's birth and death information are available at https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8231462/abigail-king
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LH1F-KD7
2 CONT * "The Descendants of Thomas and Richard Brush of Huntington, Long Island" fiche 6048615. p. 88. Fanny Reynolds, dau of Benjamin Brush and Samantha Reynolds, b. abt 1786, m. 28 Dec 1806 William Rundle (bap. 27 Mar. 1768) son of Ja
2 CONC cob Rundle and Rebecca Knapp. Fanny d. 1 May 1865.
