1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NExt to youngest child in a fam of 12 children. The parents, 5 brothers, and 6 sisters all preceded her in death.  She was 9 when the parents passed away in the winter of 1879. She went to Harlan, Shelby County, IA
2 CONC  to live with relatives -- according to obit elder sisters Married 2/11/1889 to Otis Westrope at Harlan Co, IA to that union 3 children were born: Velma Lula, Vernor Otis, and Doris Levern 2/22/1889 she and Otis came to farm in Li
2 CONC ncoln Township Adams Co IA to live. Lived there over 50 yrs and improved prarie land into a good home.  Charter memebers of Lincoln Center Church, church was held in schoolhouse She was a teacher in the sunday school for over 36 y
2 CONC rs, always ready to help with anything that was for the good of the community and to help her neighbors when needing help She filled in a mothers place to 2 little nephews, 6 and 4 years old. Lawrence Kemp and Herbert Kemp -- they
2 CONC  lived in the home until grown young men -- from obit: Sister died in 1890.  She lived on farm 6 years alon after death of Husband in 1939.  June 26 1946 she bought a home and moved to corning. She loved to be busy with her flower
2 CONC s and enjoyed outdoors Mr Westrope and the 2 daughters preceded her in death. The son Vernor lives at Lincoln, NE and there are 6 grandchildren: Warren Evans, Stanley Evans, Perry Westrope, MErrill Westrope, Delores Westrope Bargm
2 CONC an, and Margaret Westrope. 12 great grandchildren
2 CONT
