1 NAME Lynne /Rich/
2 GIVN Lynne
2 SURN Rich
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 JAN 1933
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 OCT 2015
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/153493822/lynne-rich
2 CONT
2 CONT Lynne Rich January 19, 1933 ~ October 6, 2015 (age 82)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lynne Rich was a faithful and beloved mother, grand-mother and great-grandmother, and a sweet and sensitive care-giver and friend.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lynne graduated from Ogden High School, studied at Utah State University, and University of Utah, earning a B.S. degree in Home Economics in 1956. She married Robert Eugene Lichfield (deceased) of Ogden Utah, September 10, 1954, i
2 CONC n the Salt Lake City Temple, and divorced in 1984.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lynne and Robert spent time in Texas, stationed with the Air Force, then back to Ogden,
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1957, at the birth of their first child, Aaron. With Aaron, Kathryn and Emily in tow, Lynne and Robert then moved to Menlo Park, California in 1964, where she had her last two children, and made life-long friends, raising her f
2 CONC amily in California, for 12 years. She moved back to Ogden, to be with her mother after her father's death, in 1976, and stayed until 1994, when she moved with Diana, to Logan and then, North Logan, Utah. In 2007, she moved to Poi
2 CONC nt Loma, in San Diego, California, seeking a warmer climate for herself and Diana, which she enjoyed until her passing; making annual summer visits to Bear Lake, in Fish Haven, Idaho; never missing a year.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a devoted lifelong companion and daily caregiver for her daughter, Diana, from the early 1990's, until Diana's recent death in January of 2014. She was assisted in this calling, by her children, Aaron and Sara; and by her 
2 CONC friends, Liliana Regino and Ana Estrada, who, later assisted with her own care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lynne focused her thoughts on helping others; and prioritized her energies and resources to serve wherever she sensed a need. She had a strong testimony of the gospel of Jesus Christ, and served in many callings in the LDS church 
2 CONC including compassionate service director, pianist, visiting teacher, and Young Women President. She was an excellent cook, and pursued her interests by reading about nutrition, psychology, gospel topics, and scriptures, and by sup
2 CONC porting cultural events, cooking and cleaning for loved ones, and taking walks.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her ex-husband Robert Lichfield, and her youngest daughter Diana Lichfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her son, Aaron Rich Lichfield, (DeAnn Gittins ) of North Logan; her daughters, Kathryn Lichfield of Salt Lake City, Emily Lichfield Cannon,( Scott ) of Bountiful, Sara Lichfield of San Diego, California; 10 gran
2 CONC d-children, and 12 great-grand children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services will be held on Saturday, October 17, 2015 at 11 a.m. at the Malan’s Peak Ward Chapel, 1643 26th Street, Ogden; with the viewing from 9:45 to 10:45 a.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment, Ogden City Cemetery, Rich family plot. In Lieu of flowers, donations can be made to Primary Children’s Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary, Lindquist Mortuaries
