1 OCCU Cabinet-maker, fuller, factory owner
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Stephen Joseph Abbott''', son of  James Abbott (1753 - 1830) and Phoebe Howe Coray (1763 - 1842), was born 16 August 1804 at Providence, Lancaster County, Pennsylvania and died 19 October 1844 at Nauvoo, Hancock
2 CONC  County, Illinois. Stephen was six feet tall, strongly built, with black hair and brown eyes. On 11 December 1825, he married '''Abigail Smith''' (1806 - 1889), daughter of James Smith and Lydia Lucinda Harding, in Dansville, Steu
2 CONC ben County, New York. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After their marriage Stephen went into the cabinetmaking business with Samuel A. Smith. Two year later Stephen bought Smith's share of the business and brought his brother James into the partnership. At various times Stephen also 
2 CONC owned and operated a cording and fulling machine, a yarn factory, and a potash boiling business. In 1830 Stephen decided to move west. He booked passage for his family on a boat down the Allegheny River and they arrived in Pike Co
2 CONC unty, Illinois after a five- week trip. He purchased a quarter-section farm and 40 acres of timberland near Perry, Pike County, where he built a log house with a dirt roof. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In this small cabin their sixth child was born. Abigail wrote of the event,"On the 1st day of December of that year our son Myron was born, a promising child. My daughters went out in the garden and found a beautiful rose, althoug
2 CONC h the season for that flower was long past. I took it as a good omen of promise and rejoiced." Stephen eventually built a two-story frame house along with a furniture shop and woolen factory there in Perry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Religion was never an important part of Stephen' life until his marriage to Abigail. At 17 she experienced a dream in which she saw a large company of people dressed in white, singing a song which sounded more glorious than any so
2 CONC ng she had ever heard before. After their marriage, they joined a religious sect called the Universalists. In 1839 they joined the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. In 1842, they moved to Nauvoo, Hancock County, Illinoi
2 CONC s to be with the Saints there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Myron wrote of his father: "My father operated a yarn factory and cabinet shop in Perry County, Illinois. When I was 2 years old a man named Joseph Wood came to the area preaching the gospel of Christ. My father Stephen Abbott wen
2 CONC t to hear him preach and embraced the gospel. My Father moved to Nauvoo in 1842 and in 1843 was called on a mission to the Southern States. In order to fulfill his mission he with several other brethren went to rafting lumber down
2 CONC  the Mississippi River to obtain means to support their families in their absence. He took ill and died of pneumonia when I was 8 years old. He was a kind husband and indulgent father and a true latter-day saint, ever willing to r
2 CONC espond to every call that was made upon him by the authority of the Church. He was much respected by all who knew him. He owned property in Nauvoo, stock in the Nauvoo House, and worked on the Nauvoo Temple. He and Lyman Wight own
2 CONC ed property at the Apperstone Steamboat Landing on the Mississippi Just north of the Nauvoo rapids."
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS Prophet Joseph Smith spoke at Stephen's funeral, saying that Stephen had been called on the other side to fill his mission. Stephen Joseph Abbott was buried in an unmarked grave in Nauvoo. When Abigail was forced to leave Nauv
2 CONC oo with her family, she recorded, "I had no means to erect a monument, or even a slab to mark my beloved one's grave, but I planted some morning glory on the grave and left him there to sleep and rest." 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriage and Children==
2 CONT '''Abigail Smith Abbott''' (1806 - 1889)
2 CONT #Emily Abbott (1827 - 1913)
2 CONT #Charilla Abbott (4 July 1829 - 10 April 1914)
2 CONT #Phoebe Abigail Abbott  (18 May 1831 Hornellsville, Steuben County, New York - 9 January 1914 Thatcher, Graham County, Arizona)
2 CONT #Lydia Lucinda Abbott (25 February 1833 - 18 September 1919)
2 CONT #Abiel Abbott (10 July 1835 - 2 December 1913)
2 CONT #Myron Abbott (1 December 1837 - 3 September 1907)
2 CONT #Cynthia Abbott (28 December 1839 - 14 November 1910)
2 CONT #Abigail Abbott (23 February 1842 - 25 October 1934)
2 CONT
