2 CONT
2 CONT Christina Darwin
2 CONT Alternate Names
2 CONT Christina Cooper (Married Name)
2 CONT Christina Guest Cooper (Alternate Name)
2 CONT Birth Date: 1817 March 10th
2 CONT Death Date: 1881 January 14th
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina and her children sailed to America in 1850 on the ship Argo.  Another child, Mary Elizabeth Cooper, born in 1849, was on the ship with the family, but we have not been able to determine if she survived and came to Utah w
2 CONC ith the family.  Family tradition says that her husband James came to America in 1847.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Kimberworth, Yorkshire, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth Law
2 CONT Father: John Darwin 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married James Cooper: 1835 December 25 (Age 18)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized: 1843 September 9 (Age 26)
2 CONT
2 CONT Traveled in Moses Clawson Company (1853)
2 CONT 1853 May 21 – September 15 (Age 36) Pioneers in Company
2 CONT
2 CONT Traveling Group
2 CONT Joseph Guest Cooper (Age 9)
2 CONT James Cooper (Age 44)
2 CONT Caroline Cooper (Age 16)
2 CONT Frederick Guest Cooper (Age 15)
2 CONT Sarah Ann Cooper (Age 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in Wellsville, Cache, Utah Territory, United States
2 CONT 1881 January 14 (Age 63)
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Clawson Company (1853)
2 CONT Departed: On 1853 May 21
2 CONT Departed From: Keokuk, Iowa
2 CONT Arrived: On 1853 September 15
2 CONT Vehicle Type: Wagon
2 CONT Company Type: Church Train
2 CONT Company Direction:Westbound
2 CONT
2 CONT 294 individuals and 56 wagons were in the company when the roster was created on  it began its journey from the outfitting post at Keokuk, Iowa. Four babies were born on the trail. The company was organized at Kanesville, Iowa (pr
2 CONC esent day Council Bluffs, Iowa). The first people were reported to arrived in the valley as early as 15 September, but others continued to come in up until 20 September 1853.
