2 CONT From the website Find A Grave.com:  Leo F. Layton, 49, a resident of Thatcher, Arizona, died August 17, 1943, at 2:45 p.m. after being crushed between his truck and a rock while driving as a produce dealer on State Route 82, seven
2 CONC  miles east of Pagonia.  He is the son of Fred Layton and Barbara McGuire Layton.  He served in World War I as a private in the 134th Infantry 34th Division. He left behind his loving wife Laura Layton.  Carroon Mortuary handled t
2 CONC he funeral arrangements.
