1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Three years after the death of her first husband, Isles Merion Rollins, Sr., in 1941, Esma Cynthia Layton Rollins married Elmer Alexander, who died in 1969.  Esma herself passed away in 1972 in Sonoma County, Calif
2 CONC ornia.  Esma and Iles had one daughter, Ruth Marian Rollins Aide.  Esma was a granddaughter of a famous Mormon Pioneer, Pvt. Christopher Layton who practiced polygamy, had 10 wives and 65 children.  Esma's first husband, Isles Mer
2 CONC ion Rollins, was the grandson of James Henry Rollins, who was another early Mormon Pioneer husband to two wives and 23 children.  
