2 ADDR
3 CITY Thatcher Cemetery
3 STAE Arizona Territory
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Agnes married Heber C. Layton
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AGNES LAYTON FUNERAL HELD:  THATCHER, Nov. 10--Funeral services for Mrs. Agnes Alameda Layton, pioneer resident of the Gila Valley, who died at the family home here, November 5, were held Monday at the Latter-Day S
2 CONC aints Chapel here under the direction of Eldon Painter.  Speakers at the service were Harry L. Payne and Jack Daley and music was furnished by the Thatcher Third Ward Singing Mothers and Evan A. Madsen.  Mrs. Layton was born Novem
2 CONC ber 19, 1867, in Bloomington, Idaho and came to Gila Valley in 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, Heber C. Layton; six grandchildren, Heber L. Layton, Miami;  Agnes Romney and Della Smith, Los Angeles;  Roy A. Layton, Thatcher;  Glenna Smoals, Farmington, New Mexico, and Genieve Clifford, Safford; si
2 CONC x brothers, Robert Welker, Arthur Welker and Elmer Welker, Safford; Adam Welker and Delbert Welker, Los Angeles, and William Welker, Phoenix, and two sisters, Mrs. J. E. Zundail, Phoenix, and Mrs. B. F. Peel, Los Angeles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arizona Republic, pg. 2, sec. 2, Nov. 11, 1943, transcribed by Rhonda Holton
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. AGNES LAYTON:  Agnes Almeda Layton, age 75, a long time resident of Thatcher, Arizona, died November 5, 1943 due to complications from bronchial pneumonia.  Her parents were Adam Welker and Agnes Dock Welker.  She spent most 
2 CONC of her life being a housewife and mother.  Surviving her is her husband Heber Layton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Welker (1841 - 1926)
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Dock Welker (1847 - 1913)
2 CONT
