1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Annie Elizabeth Brady is the third child and first daughter in a family of eleven children. Her parents are Simeon Henderson Brady and Annie Ostensen. she married Franklin D. White October 16 1907 in the Manti Temp
2 CONC le. They lived for a time in Indianola, UT. Their first two sons, Alden D. and Ewin Ariston were born there. Then they moved to Hazelton, Idaho to farm. Simeon Woodrow, Lowell Franklin and Leatha Liverda were born there. Elizabeth
2 CONC  missed Utah so finally they moved back. Newell Junior and Anna Vonda were born in Mt. Pleasant Utah. Elizabeth was very ill after Vonda's birth. She received a blessing promising that she would live to raise her children which sh
2 CONC e did. The family moved to McKinnon Wyoming where some of Elizabeth' brothers had settled.
2 CONT Elizabeth was a hard worker. She always welcomed family and friends to her home. She loved flowers She liked to do fancy work of all kinds and made many things that added to the beauty and comfort of their home. Her son Aristol pa
2 CONC ssed on March 16, 1928. After the family was raised Franklin and Elizabeth moved to Provo Utah.Elizabeth passed away at home in Provo, Utah at the age of 66 years, 7 months, and 6 days.
