1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Created from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=145631321-7-25238&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-3781df005c9259e8ef2e7c77661afabb&mrid=1e43ba069baae4972b8e
2 CONC d253b3182145 MyHeritage Match] via brother [http://www.geni.com/profile-34663974235 Thaddeus Walton] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 4 2014, 1:09:01 UTC''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/155778622/donal-walton
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Donal Walton was born October 21, 1884, in Woodruff to Wesley K. Walton and Frances M. Huffaker, the fifth child of a family of thirteen.  He died December 12, 1958.  He attended the public schools in Woodruff and Salt Lake City a
2 CONC nd also the Utah State Agricultural College at Logan, Utah.  Leah Dickson and he were married February 8, 1916. They had one child, Layne, and three grandchildren.  Doan spent a large portion of his life on the ranch at Woodruff.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father had stocked the ranch with a large number of purebred Shorthorn cattle and Doan had most of the responsibility of caring for these and keeping records of them.  They were an excellent strain of Shorthorns and for many y
2 CONC ears we sold bulls for breeding purposes in many places in Utah, Wyoming and Idaho.  Doan and Leah lived at the ranch while it was still a family home for some of us.  Leah was an excellent cook and housekeeper and it fell her lot
2 CONC  to cook and keep house for the rest of us which she did, and Doan also, in a gracious and accommodating manner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doan had an excellent memory and we all felt that if he remembered a thing a certain way it could be accepted as a fact.  Doan, along with Lester and Hannah, was always exceptionally good to mother.  Not only in little ways but in
2 CONC  seeing she had things she needed.  For example when it was discovered that open cars were pretty cold to travel in, he saw that she had a new “glassed in” sedan.  This was in 1919.  If she needed a new stove or anything he would 
2 CONC see that she got it.  He bought for our ranch home one of the first phonographs and one of the first cream separators that were on the market.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doan and Leah were divorced and Doan and Layne moved to Salt Lake City where Doan worked for the Ken Garff Automobile Company and Layne went to high school.
2 CONT
2 CONT April 19, 1943, Donal and Gladys Laura Parry were married in the Salt Lake Temple.  Gladys was a school teacher in the Granite School District at Salt Lake.  They were always very happy together and had a nice home in Salt Lake wh
2 CONC ere Gladys still lives.  Doan and Gladys have always been very active in the LDS Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT By Arthur Walton, from "The First 100 Years in Woodruff", printed by Art City Publishing Co., Springville, Utah, 1972, pages 472-4
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary from a local newspaper:  Donal (Doan) Walton, 74, 1004 E. 45th South, died Friday at 2:30 p.m. at his residence of a heart ailment.  Born October 21, 1884, in Woodruff, Rich County, Utah.  He was a rancher until 1940 when
2 CONC  he moved to Salt Lake City.
