1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT July 31, 1913, Thursday, Cassville Republican, Barry Co., MO
2 CONT Presidents and Clerks of School Boards
2 CONT Held an interesting Meeting Monday
2 CONT The meeting of the presidents and clerks of school bards held at the Baptist church in Cassville Monday was largely attend and proved to be one of much interest. [content of meeting not included]
2 CONT The following presidents and school clerks were present from the various districts of the county:
2 CONT Cedar Mound, B. R. Stumpff, clerk, Cato; J. N. Hudson, pres., Jenkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cassville Republican, Thursday, June 6, 1946
2 CONT Benjamin Robert Stumpff was born April 21, 1874, in Dade County, Mo. He was the son of F.M. and Sally E. Stumpff.
2 CONT He passed away May 29, at the home of his daughter, Mrs. Erma Padgett, at the age of 72 years, 1 month, and 8 days.
2 CONT Mr. Stumpff came to Barry county at the age of 19 years and lived here the remainder of his life.
2 CONT He was married to Sarah Lillie Hudson December 15, 1901.
2 CONT He is survived by four sons, three daughters: Miles Stumpff, Mesa, Wash.; Roy, Bill, Mrs. Clema Cope, Mrs. Clara Elliott and Burl of Bakersfield, Calif.; and Mrs. Erma Padget; three brothers, one sister, George Stumpff, Galena, Mo
2 CONC .; Charley Stumpff, Cape Fair, Mo.; Frank Stumpff, Cassville and Mrs. Maggie Bailie, Pasco, Wash.
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted by Rev. Robinson at the Clio church Sunday, June 2, 3 p.m. with burial in Clio cemetery under direction of Koon Funeral Home.
