1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT Stone County News-Oracle, Friday, August 30, 1957
2 CONT Charlie B. Stumpff, 72, died at his home at Cape Fair, Mo., Monday afternoon at 6:15.
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, Allie of the home; one daughter, Mrs. Noveta Williamson of Los Angeles, Calif.; one son, Aubrey Stumpff of the home; one sister, Mrs. Maggie Bailey of Pasco, Wash.; one brother, Frankie Stumpff of Rocky
2 CONC  Comfort, Mo.; and three grandchildren.
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Thursday afternoon at 2:30 in the Clio Church, with burial in the church cemetery under direction of the Manlove Funeral home of Crane, Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stone County News-Oracle, Friday, September 6, 1957
2 CONT Charley Barkley Stumpff, youngest son of Frances and Sarah Stumpff was born March 31, 1885 in Johnson Co., Mo., and departed this life August 26, 1957, at his home, Cape Fair, Mo., at the age of 72 years, 4 months and 26 days.
2 CONT In early childhood he moved with his parents to Barry County, Missouri.
2 CONT He was united in marriage to Allie Ennis, Dec. 13, 1909. To this union two children were born.
2 CONT As a young man he became a member of the Church of Christ and remained a faithful member.
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, Allie; a daughter, Mrs. Onen Williamson, Los Angeles, Calif.; a son Aubrey Stumpff, Cape Fair, Mo.; three grandchildren, Bobby Dean Leonard, of the U.S. Marine Corp., Ruth Ann Leonard and Charlene Stump
2 CONC ff; a sister, Mrs. Maggie Bailie, Pasco, Wash.; a brother, Frank Stumpff, Rocky Comfort, Mo.
2 CONT C.B. as he was known by his relatives and friends had lived on his farm in Dry Hollow for 47 years and will be missed by all.
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted at 2:30 o'clock Thursday afternoon at Clio. Morton Woodard of Cassville officiated. Burial was in the Clio cemetery, under direction of Manlove Funeral Home of Crane, Mo.
