1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT October 10, 1912, Thursday, Cassville Republican, Barry Co., MO
2 CONT The many friends of Frank Stumpff, who went to Kansas City, last week to have his eyes treated, will be grieved to learn that he was compelled to have his right eye removed. His left eye is also in critical condition and it may gi
2 CONC ve him total blindness.
2 CONT
2 CONT January 9, 1913, Thursday, Cassville Republican, Barry Co., MO
2 CONT Frank Stumpff returned from Kansas City, Wednesday of last week where he has been for several weeks to have his eyes treated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cassville Republican, Thursday, January 8, 1959
2 CONT RITES HERE MONDAY FOR MARION F STUMPFF
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted Monday afternoon at the Cassville Church of Christ for Marion Francis Stumpff, 86 years old, who died Thursday afternoon. Mr. Stumpff who had been blind for many years, passed away at the home of Fr
2 CONC ank Garrett near Rocky Comfort where he had made his home for the past five years. He had been in ill health for several years.
2 CONT Born April 1, 1872 in Dade County, Mo., he came to Barry county in 1893, where he was engaged in farming.
2 CONT Surviving are a daughter, Mrs. Nellie Lassiter of Bakersfield, Calif.; one sister, Mrs. Maggie Bailie of Pasco, Wash.; and several nieces and nephews.
2 CONT Bro. Keith Marshall officiated at the service and burial was in the Mineral Springs cemetery under direction of the Williamson Chapel in the Valley of Cassville.
