1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Marriages Sep 1849===
2 CONT * Hawkins	 Angelina	 	 St.Pancras	 1	389	 
2 CONT * Piercy	 Frederick	 	 St Pancras	 1	389
2 CONT
2 CONT http://mormonhistoricsites.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/04/MHS_Fall2003_Frederick-Piercy.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.lds.org/ensign/2000/07/chronicling-the-journey-to-zion?lang=eng
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Born on 27 January 1830 in Portsea, Hampshire, England, to '''George and Deborah Adams Piercy,''' Frederick was baptized on 23 March 1848 and served a mission to Paris in 1850. He married Angelina Hawkins on 15 September 1849, a
2 CONC nd they became the parents of 11. Sadly, in 1857 they left the Church due to misunderstandings surrounding the publication of his book. However, his sister Syrina immigrated to Utah with her husband, Thomas Biggs, and remained fai
2 CONC thful to the Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Piercy continued to exhibit his art in London. In 1881 Angelina died. Three years later, though stricken with paralysis, he married artist Catherine Wornum, and they had one son. Piercy died on 10 June 1891".
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Further References and Sources
