1 NAME Martha Patsy /Rice/
2 GIVN Martha Patsy
2 SURN Rice
2 _MARNM Atwell
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 DEC 1769
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 DEC 1819
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 FAMS @F6000000009379290253@
1 RFN geni:6000000009379290249
1 SUBM @S6000000000212306108@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Ancestry Family Trees
1 NOTE The following is from Vickie Leedy, probably via Lois Kimmons:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Atwell Sr. and John Atwell Jr. moved to Caswell Co. North Carolinaabout 1797. Martha (Rice) Atwell wife of John Atwell Jr. died in CaswellCo. NC, from burns on Dec 25, 1819 in her home. Her dress caught firewhile she was cook
2 CONC ing at the fireplace. There were several people at herhome at the time, as indicated by the Coroner's inquest. At the inquestwere, Benjamin Johnston, Nancy Johnston, Mary Johnston, Mary Yokley,Nancy Page, John Mason, Joshua Beavel
2 CONC , John Harris Sr., Joseph Atwell,Henry Atwell, James Stafford, Mary Stafford and Douglas Fulcher. DouglasFulcher was married to John and Martha's oldest daughter Nancy (m. 2 Oct1816). Nancy was expecting a child in the near future
2 CONC  and was unable tobe questioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has always been confusing that the family was pretty well documentedin Person county, but that they seem to have been living in CaswellCounty at the time of the accident.  They would have to have movedbetween the 1816 marriage 
2 CONC of Nancy and the 1819 fire.  Helping to showthat this is the family that was previously in Person County is thefinding of the 1805 census/tax list for Person Co.  (My image 460)  Itshows John Atwell with zero acres of land and he 
2 CONC is the only male over21.  The part of the list that I copied only contains a portion of thecounty - Capt. Sargent's Company.  Besides John the Company comprised atleast three of the witnesses to the fire listed above.  The Atwells
2 CONC  musthave moved to Caswell and shortly after had their former neighbors overfor Christmas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathy,
2 CONT
2 CONT   I have Martha as daughter of Joseph, Jr.  First, she is not mentionedin the will of Joseph, Sr. probated 1766.  There could be reasons forthat but the simplest explanation is that she is not his daughter.Second, there is the mar
2 CONC riage record:
2 CONT
2 CONT 'John, son of John, Sr., m. 22 Dec., 1796, Patsy Rice, dau. of Joseph.Sur (surety), John Atwell.  Prince Edward County Marriage Record.'
2 CONT
2 CONT   It's unusual for the record to mention Joseph if he were dead for 30years.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Third, John Atwell was 23 when he married so it would have beenunexpected for him to have married someone at least 30.
2 CONT
2 CONT   All in all, it's circumtantial, but I think that Martha is the daughterof Joseph, Jr.  There is no other record of his children....yet.  He soldhis land in Prince Edward about 1798 and I don't know where he ended up.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ray
1 CHAN
2 DATE 03 MAY 2022
3 TIME 19:01:03
0 @I6000000000892415873@ INDI
