1 FAMS @F6000000009379290253@
1 RFN geni:6000000000892415873
1 SUBM @S6000000000212306108@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Kentucky Land Grants
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL 1830 United States Federal Census
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL 1820 United States Federal Census
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL 1810 United States Federal Census
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Ancestry Family Trees
1 NOTE Following is a quotation from 'Marriages of Some Virginia Residents,1607-1800' by D.F. Wulfeck:
2 CONT 'John, son of John, Sr., m. 22 Dec., 1796, Patsy Rice, dau. of Joseph.Sur (surety), John Atwell.  Prince Edward County Marriage Record.'
2 CONT
2 CONT John is later found in the 1800 census for Person County, North Carolina,and is still there in 1810.  (My images 222 and 59 ) (During the sameperiod there is a John Sr and John Jr in the adjacent Caswell County.(My image 53)  As o
2 CONC f late 2004 I don't know how they relate to ourbranch.  Some time between the 1816 marriage of Nancy  in Person Co. andMartha's accidental death in 1819, the family must have moved to CaswellCounty, because that is where the accid
2 CONC ent took place.
2 CONT
2 CONT As further confirmation that the Person County John is ours, there is aJohn Atwell in Capt. Sergent's company of the militia in 1805 in PersonCounty.  (No land for tax purposes which agrees with our lack offindings in the Person C
2 CONC ounty court house.)  Named in the same smallcompany are at least four men who where present at Martha's death asshown in the inquest report.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clearing up one other little confusing detail - several other researchershave posted information noting that a John Atwell sold land in Illinoisto a John Wilson in 1819 and recorded the transfer in Person County.  Theland was from
2 CONC  a bounty for service during the War of 1812.  I got therecords from NARA and found that the Atwell veteran was age 55 whendischarged in 1815, meaning that he was born in 1760.  Per the HoraceAtwell Bible our John was born in 1773
2 CONC .  It must have just been acoincidence that the deed transfer was recorded in Person County.Besides, while at least three of John's relatives were in the Army(Francis D., Charles and Booker) all enlisted from Prince Edward County,
2 CONC VA.  There seems to be no record of a John Atwell enlisting from there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other researchers have indicated that following Martha's death in 1819John Jr moved to Virginia with daughter Nancy and her husband DouglasFulcher.  In 1820 the Fulchers are found in Wythe County, VA, but thereare no John Atwells 
2 CONC indexed in that area.  However, there is a 'JohnAdwell', age greater than 45, in the very same township as the Fulchers.(My image 192)  Given that there is not a single Adwell in all of the USin 1800 or 1810, I suspect that this i
2 CONC s John Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is also a John Atwell b. 1770-1780 in the 1830 census for HenryCounty, Virginia.  There are two women in the household, one b. 1800-1810and the other b. 1770-1780.  The older was too old to be Agnes Martin, soI don't know wh
2 CONC o this family was, but the location was generally betweenCaswell County, NC and Smyth County, VA.  A find in 2005 is that a JohnAtwell died in the Washington County, Virginia poor house in February1844.  Since our John was clearly
2 CONC  not well off in his younger days, thismay well have been him.  'Washington County Virginia Minutes of The Boardof Overseers of the Poor 1826-1863'
2 CONT
2 CONT Other researchers believe that John moved to Kentucky.  There is a Johnin Green County,KY, aged greater than 45, in 1820.  (My image 218)  Ibelieve that this is the other John Jr - the one who left quite a trailof records in Caswe
2 CONC ll County, NC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date taken from the Horace Atwell Bible.
2 CONT
2 CONT Further on the Poor House issue:
2 CONT 'Unfiled Court Records' Washington Sty VA 'Old 38 Papers' Court Orders1773-1871
2 CONT      Vol 7 Part 1 - delinquents in county levy and poor 1835:
2 CONT                     Atwell, Henry   $1.10
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     $1.10
2 CONT                Rates of 1836 in Parker Smith's district:
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     1/18 3/4
2 CONT      Vol 7 Part 2 - Poor rates of 1841 in Jonathan King's district:
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     $ .75
2 CONT                     Atwell, Henry    $ .75
2 CONT
2 CONT It would seem that not only John was poor, but also son William Henry.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 06 OCT 2025
3 TIME 04:41:58
