2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Ancestry Family Trees
1 NOTE As of 2005 it is still an assumption that Joseph is a son of John Jr.,but it's a reasonable assumption.  At the inquest for Martha (Rice)Atwell's death, it was noted that Joseph and Henry Atwell had beenpresent.  These are believe
2 CONC d to be her sons.  When Joseph, William HENRY,and Nancy all are found in 1850 within a stone's throw of each other, andthey are of the right age, it is a safe assumption that they are allbrothers and sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and family are found in the 1840 (my image 108) and 1850 (my image109/110) census for Smyth Co, VA.  I have not been able to find them in1830.  Correction: During the 2006 Virginia trip, I found a Joseph in1830 Washington C
2 CONC ounty.  (My image 848.)  He has
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 males <5        (James E. and William)
2 CONT 1 male 20-30     (Joseph)
2 CONT 1 female 5-10    (Eliza Jane)
2 CONT 1 female 15-20  ??
2 CONT 1 female 20-30  Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT During the same trip, we found a publication ('Wythe County, VirginiaMarriages 1790-1853' by Vogt and Kethley, my image 851) which speculatesthat Mary's maiden name might have been Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1840 the census reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 males <5       (b. 1835-1840  John and Robert P.)
2 CONT 1 male 5-10      (b. 1830-1835  Joseph H.)
2 CONT 2 males 10-15  (b. 1825-1830  James E. and William B.)
2 CONT 1 male 30-40    (b. 1800-1810  Joseph)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 female <5       (b. 1835-1840  Martha Ann)
2 CONT 1 female 5-10    (b. 1830-1835  Sarah Susan)
2 CONT 1 female 15-20  (b. 1820-1825  Eliza Jane)
2 CONT 1 female 30-40  (b. 1800-1810  Mary)
2 CONT
2 CONT   Joseph is listed as being a carpenter.  In comparing the numbers ofchildren in 1840 vs. 1850, they look like there was an excellent survivalrate, apparently not losing any during that period.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lois Kimmons initially said that Joseph died in Cabarrus County, NorthCarolina, in 1865.  That now appears to have been a different Joseph.  In1850 our Joseph and Mary were in Smyth County, while at the same timethere were a Josep
2 CONC h and Mary in Cabarrus County, North Carolina.  (Myimage 207)  The VA family included James born about 1825, while the Jamesin the NC family had a James born about 1832.  We know from severalcensus pages that our James was born in
2 CONC  1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on census pages for his children from 1880/1900 I can'tconclusively say whether Joseph was born in Virginia or in NorthCarolina.  The following census images say it was VA: 262, 058, 302,036.  These pages say it was NC: 020,
2 CONC  304, 301.  The only page availablefor Joseph himself is from 1850, and it says VA.  (My image 109)
2 CONT
2 CONT The following were found in the Smyth County courthouse:
2 CONT
2 CONT B1 p 224 - Aug 12, 1834 John Baber Tr (ee) Joseph Atwell (or) real andpers N F Hols for $100 land on NF Holston and cows, tools, household andkitchen furniture, ...
2 CONT
2 CONT B1 p409a - Joseph Atwell (ee), Samuel Graham (or) April 5, 1834 - 100 acfor $100 in Smyth Co in ridge between the Cove and river.
2 CONT
2 CONT B3 p 26 -  Oct 3, 1840  Joseph Atwell (ee), Samuel Johnston (or) D of T,personal for $1: grey mare with colt; 2 bay horses; 1 chestnut sorrelhorse; 1 horse colt - sorrel; cattle; horse wagon; sheep; still and tubs;2 plows; 300 bus
2 CONC hels corn; hogs; household goods. Held in trust until$150 debt paid to Patrick Buchannon.
2 CONT
2 CONT B4 p 9 - April 5, 1844  William H. Atwell (ee); Joseph and Mary Atwell(or) 15 ac in Cove Ridge for $60 - part of land bought from Samuel Graham.
2 CONT
2 CONT B4 p 136 - July 7, 1845 Aaron Sexton Tr. (ee), Sexton V. Gibboney (ee),Joseph Sexton (ee) and Joseph Atwell (or) Personal. Atwell indebted to 3in sum of $44.45. Gave property (horses, cows, hogs, ...) to pay debt.
2 CONT
2 CONT B4 p 284 - Aug 22, 1846 Aaron and Joseph Sexton (ee) Joseph Atwell (or)100 ac land to settle debt.
2 CONT
2 CONT B4 p 463 - Dec 8, 1847 VS Morgan (ee) Joseph and Mary Atwell (or) Josephheld property from Sam. Graham now conveying for $1 to VS Morgan.
2 CONT
2 CONT B4 p 490 - Oct 18, 1847 Aaron Sexton (ee) Joseph and Mary Atwell (or) 100ac NF Hols paid Aaron $1 to hold land in trust to settle debt with Sextonand Gibboney.
2 CONT
2 CONT B5 p 84 - Nov 20, 1848  Joseph Atwell (ee) Soloman Crabtree (or) personal3rd party James R Crabtree, $1 - property held in trust for debt of $100
2 CONT
2 CONT B5 p 143 - May 1, 1849 William H. Spiller (ee) Joseph Atwell (or) 100 acNF Hols
2 CONT Joseph, brother of William H. Atwell ...   15 ac from Jos to WH Atwell,rest sold for $150 to Spiller to settle debt with Sexton and Gibboney.
2 CONT
2 CONT See my image 869 for further detail on the first entry.  Joseph seems tohave had financial trouble and sold land an his carpenter's tools tosettle a debt.  And see my image 870 for further sale information fromitem two.
2 CONT
2 CONT The final entry confirms that William H. (Henry) was a brother to Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT We have their marriage record.  In it Joseph is listed as Joseph Adwell,but it's a safe assumption that it's really Atwell.  My image 822.
