1 NOTE As of 2005 it is still an assumption that William Henry is a son of JohnJr., but it's a reasonable assumption.  At the inquest for Martha (Rice)Atwell's death, it was noted that Joseph and Henry Atwell had beenpresent.  These are 
2 CONC believed to be her sons.  When Joseph, William HENRY,and Nancy all are found in 1850 within a stone's throw of each other, andthey are of the right age, it is a safe assumption that they are allbrothers and sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Listed in the 1850 census for Smyth Co, VA, with much of the family.Shown nearby are Douglas and Nancy Fulcher and Benjamin McCrary andBarbara Fulcher Pritchett.  (My image 319 and 764)  Still in Smyth Co in1860 (My image 085) whe
2 CONC re William is now 60 years old.  By 1870 Margaretis living with son John in West Virginia.  (My image 061) and is presumedto be a widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from the Stallards indicates that William and Margaretmarried in Washington County, Virginia before 1831.  'Marriage: Bef.1831, Washington County, Virginia (Source: FamilySearch.com.)'  It wouldbe interesting if this w
2 CONC ere true because it adds further ties to Eli whowas found there, as well as to the John Atwell who died there in the poorhouse.  (See notes under John Jr.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Sherynn Atwell Stallard:
2 CONT      According to oral family history, William Henry Atwell was alsocalled John Henry Atwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Smyth County Deed Books:
2 CONT
2 CONT B19 p 136 - J L Woodall (ee) William H. Atwell (by clerk) (or) Sold 31 acof land of Wm H Atwell estate at public auction for back taxes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Found during our 2006 visit:
2 CONT 'Unfiled Court Records' Washington Sty VA 'Old 38 Papers' Court Orders1773-1871
2 CONT      Vol 7 Part 1 - delinquents in county levy and poor 1835:
2 CONT                     Atwell, Henry   $1.10
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     $1.10
2 CONT                Rates of 1836 in Parker Smith's district:
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     1/18 3/4
2 CONT      Vol 7 Part 2 - Poor rates of 1841 in Jonathan King's district:
2 CONT                     Atwell, John     $ .75
2 CONT                     Atwell, Henry    $ .75
