1 NOTE There is no conclusive evidence that Eli is the son of John Jr. andbrother to Nancy, Joseph and William Henry.  Eli's birth in NorthCarolina at a time when John and Patsy were there, combined with hispresence in Smyth County in 18
2 CONC 50 along with the others makes it a goodbet, however.  More recently, there was the discovery that a John Atwelldied in the poor house in Washington County in 1844 - at about the timethat Eli was there - helps to support the possi
2 CONC ble relationship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eli and Nancy are in 1850 Smyth County, Virginia.  Living with them areRobert (19), Martha (17), and James (15) 'Bowls'  I wondered if Marthamight be an older daughter of Eli/Nancy who had married Robert Bowls, butthen I don't kno
2 CONC w how James fits in... brother of Robert?  (My image 320)  Later: I've found Eli/Nancy in the 1840 census for Washington County,Virginia,  (my image 886) where the whole family is listed as FreeColored Persons, apparently includin
2 CONC g Eli.  The report was 3 males under10; 1 male 10-24; 1 male 24-36; 1 female under 10 (could very well beMartha); and 1 female 36-55.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870 they have moved to Jackson Township, Pike County, Ohio, and arenear son Eli2.  (My image 305)  By 1880 Eli Sr. is a widower living withthe family of Eli Jr. in Paint Township, Fayette County, Ohio.  (My image365)
2 CONT
2 CONT Eli's year of birth is in question.  Here is what is found on the variouscensus pages: 1840 (born between 1804-1816), 1850 (b. 1810), 1870 (b.1803), 1880 (b. 1804).  The family isn't found in 1860, and even thoughLinda Artis says 
2 CONC that he didn't die until 1914, he isn't indexed for 1900or 1910.  She says he was born in 1808 and is more likely than I am tohave the information.  Maybe it's on the death certificate which sheseems to have.  One problem is that 
2 CONC the 1800 and 1810 census for John andMartha only show two boys born before 1810.  (My images 222 and 059)It's more likely that those two are Joseph and William Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE THAT MUCH OF THE DETAIL ON ELI'S LINE CAME FROM A GENEALOGY POSTINGBY LINDA ARTIS OF COLUMBUS, OHIO.  MY REFERENCES TO CENSUS IMAGES SUPPORTHER INFORMATION.
