1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Neils Lomen Johnson, husband of Johanna Peterson Johnson, and father of Johanna Johnson Larsen, Matilda Johnson, Charles D. Johnson, Hilma Caroline Johnson Hales, and John A. Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born June 6th, 1822, in Hurup, Denmark. He joined the church of Jesus Christ of Later Day Saints, in Sweden about 1861 and came to Utah in the fall of 1868, with his oldest child Johanna Johnson and his wife’s sister Christ
2 CONC ina.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he arrived here he did not live with his wife and five children as his wife, as his wife and 4 of his children fad come a year earlier, settling in Spanish Fork and she had remarried in the mean time to Christian Larsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Neils Lomen Johnson worked on the railroad a few years, and then settled in Spring City, Sanpete Co, Utah. He married a widow of Peter Rockhills. She died a year later. He again married a Swedish lady by the name of Annie. They li
2 CONC ved together a long time and she died 1898. Later her son Charles moved him to Spanish Fork, in 1902 where he lived among his children until the later part of November in 1908 when he died at the age of 82 and was buried in the Sp
2 CONC anish Fork cemetery.
