1 OCCU railroad engineer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/177406493/John-Fereday
2 CONT
2 CONT A Recollection by Anna Eliza McBride Barrus
2 CONT
2 CONT My grandfather, John Bird, son of George Bird and Elizabeth Fereday, was born 19 July 1820, in Paradise, Staffordshire, England. He married Martha Lewis on 23 October 1845. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of ten children, all of whom were born in England. Six of their children, three boys and three girls, died in England. His occupation was an engineer on the railroad.
2 CONT
2 CONT The missionaries brought the Gospel to their home, and they joined the Church and came to Utah. They crossed the ocean on a steam ship, which was six weeks on the water. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They came across the plains with the first mule team company and arrived in Salt Lake in 1858. He invented a smoke consumer, which consumed the smoke in Salt Lake City. He and his family first lived in Salt Lake, then moved to St.
2 CONC  John, Utah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their first home there was a dugout, I .don't know how long they lived there but their next home was in Logan, Utah. They lived there until Grandmother's death, 29 December 1894. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandfather lived four years after she died. The last few months of his life he lived with us, and Mother took care of him. He died 18 February 1898.
