2 CONT Jan. 17, 1853: ”The State of Ohio, Morgan County SS
2 CONT
2 CONT On this 17th day of January in the year 1853, Mary Mingus came personally before me a Justice of the Peace within and for said County who being duly sworn according to law deposes and saith that that (sic.) Luther Mingus an aplica
2 CONC nt [sic.] for Bounty land in right of John Mingus deceased who was a private in Captain H. Hickman's Company of the twelfth regiment of Infantry United States Army, war of 1812 and who died in the service at Buffalo, New York, on 
2 CONC or about the 28th day of October in the year 1814. Depondent avers that she is the sister-in-law of the said applicant that affiant is the widow of Gideon, a Brother of applicant and also of the said John Mingus in whose right sai
2 CONC d land is sought to be obtained, affiant further avers that she is acquainted with the said applicant forty years that she knew the said John Mingus applicant's Brother before he went into the Army, that said Luther Mingus was alw
2 CONC ays recognized regarded and hath by their parents to be their lawful child and son of the same parents of said John Mingus, that the said Luther Mingus hath no Brother living and no sister living to the best of affiant's knowledge
2 CONC , that both the Parents of said Luther are dead and that the said Luther is to the best of affiant's knowledge and belief the only surviving heir of John Mingus aforesaid. Mary Mingus
2 CONT
2 CONT Sworn to and subscribed before me this 17th day of January A.D. 1853 James A. Adair, Justice of the Peace"
2 CONT **********************************************************************************
2 CONT January 22, 1853: Probate Court Journal, Vol. 1, p 52, Hocking Co., OH
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mingus matters.
2 CONT
2 CONT This day proof was made in open court by the affiants of Mary Mingus, Hannah Mingus & Daniel Frasure, that Luther Mingus is the only surviving brother of & him at law in fee of John Mingus decd. late a private in Capt. H. Hickman’
2 CONC s Company 17th Regt. U.S. infantry, who died in the service of the U.S. at Buffalo Oct. 28, 1814 and that he has no sister or parents now living.    F. Case, Judge
2 CONT **********************************************************************************
2 CONT Athens County Home: Athens County, OH
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Mingus of Athens Twp., Athens Co., OH.
2 CONT 72 years, born Vermont.
2 CONT January 5, 1859: Admitted.
2 CONT March 5, 1859: Taken away by son, Calvin Mingus.
2 CONT **********************************************************************************
2 CONT 1860 Census:  Eagle Twp., Vinton Co., OH, p. 246.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Vicas		41 Farmer   $500 RE  $100 PE 	OH
2 CONT Mary			39						OH
2 CONT William W.		20  Day Labor				OH
2 CONT Clarisa M.		16						OH
2 CONT Mary E.		13						OH
2 CONT Lorenzo		12						OH
2 CONT Hannah		  8						OH
2 CONT John J.		  5						OH
2 CONT Calvin		  2						OH
2 CONT Mary Mingus	73						VT
