1 CONT 6. Ransom Abraham Stevens, who was born on September
1 CONT             27, 1839, at Springfield, Ill. On February 17,
1 CONT             1836, he married Tranquilla Ann Brady, who was bo
1 CONT             on January 22, 1846 in Hancock Co., Ill. She w
1 CONT             the daughter of Lindsey Brady and Elizabeth A
1 CONT             Anderson. They had:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT             i. Ransom Marion Stevens, who was born on M
1 CONT                 1864. He married Annie Dorothea Christense
1 CONT                 She was the daughter of Frederick Christens
1 CONT                 and Christina Sophia Rasmussen. They had:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT                 (1) Stella Sophronia Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    on September 11, 1888. She died on Novemb
1 CONT                    9, 1888.
1 CONT                 (2) Ray Stevens, who was born on Octob
1 CONT                    1891 and who died on October 18, 189
1 CONT                    Fagalii, Upolu, Samoa.
1 CONT                 (3) Marion Christensen Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    on June 9, 1894, and who died on June 2
1 CONT                    1894, at Fairview.
1 CONT                 Ransom Marion Stevens, was a graduate of
1 CONT
1 CONT the Brigham Young University, at Provo, Utah, and went on a mission to the Southern States when only eighteen years old and again at the age  of thirty he went to Samoa on a mission. He  was president of the mission and died April
1 CONC  28, 1894, at Fagalii, Upolu, Samoa. The following obituary appeared in the Deseret News:   "Fagalii, Samoa, May 23, 1894. Since you last heard from this far-off land, the hand of death has taken from our midst, our honored and be
1 CONC loved president, Elder Ransom M. Stevens. He had been complaining of not feeling well for some time, and had been confined to his bed for ten days, when on the morning of Saturday, April 28th, 1894, his noble spirit was called hen
1 CONC ce, and
1 CONT                 we were left to mourn his loss, and try to comfo
1 CONT                 and console his grief-striken wif
1 CONT                      "Brother Stevens had been president of t
1 CONT                 Samoan mission for some time previous to h
1 CONT                 demise, and as president and co-laborer he w
1 CONT                 the love and admiration of all with whom he w
1 CONT                 associated."
1 CONT
1 CONT             ii. Arnold Stevens, who was born on March 2, 186
1 CONT                 at Fairview, Utah. He married Augusta Anders
1 CONT                 and they had:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT                 (1) Hans Arnold Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    February 24, 1886.
1 CONT                 (2) Ransom Abraham Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    June 30, 1889.
1 CONT                 (3) Della Augusta Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    November 5, 1891.
1 CONT                 (4) Ernest Andrew Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    October 13, 1894.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT             iii. Lindsey Absalom Stevens, who was born on Apr
1 CONT                  4, 1868. He married Louisa M. Anderson. Th
1 CONT                  had:
1 CONT
1 CONT (1) Birdie Margarette Stevens, who was born
1 CONT                    on March 2, 1892.
1 CONT                 (2) Lindsey James Stevens, who was bo
1 CONT                    January 4, 1894.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT             iv. Tabitha Elizabeth Stevens, who was born on Apr
1 CONT                 19, 1870, at Fairview, Utah. She marri
1 CONT                 Charles Oscar Peterson and they had:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT                 (1) Tranquilla Ann Peterson, who was bo
1 CONT                    June 2, 1889.
1 CONT                 (2) Obvedia Peterson, who was born on Janua
1 CONT                    15, 1891 and who died on February 10, 189
1 CONT                 (3) Carolina Peterson, who was born on Ju
1 CONT                    26, 1892.
1 CONT                 (4) Charles Oscar Peterson, who was bo
1 CONT                    November 25, 1894 and who died on De
1 CONT                    31, 1894.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT             v.  Lois Ann Stevens, who was born on April 2, 18
1 CONT                 at Fairview, Utah. She married John Myr
1 CONT                 Tanner and they had:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT                 (1) Myron Vasco Tanner, who was bo
1 CONT                    October 29, 1892.
1 CONT                 (2) Lois Geneva Tanner, who was born on Decemb
1 CONT                    23, 1894, and who died on Janua
1 CONT                    29, 1895.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT             vi. Tranquilla Ann Stevens, who was born on M
1 CONT                 10, 1874 at Fairview, Utah. She married Willi
1 CONT                 Henry Triplett.
1 CONT             vii. Justus Perry Stevens, who was born on April 1
1 CONT                 1876 at Fairview, Utah. He married Julia Et
1 CONT                 Bohney.
1 CONT             viii. Rhoda Matilda Stevens, who was born on Ju
1 CONT                  14, 1879 at Fairview Utah.
1 CONT             ix. Sophia Beatrice Stevens, who was born on Ju
1 CONT                 25, 1881.
1 CONT             x. Mary Ellen Stevens, who was born on Octob
1 CONT                15, 1883 and who died on November 17, 1883.
